":{"id":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference-24","page_id":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference#personal-settings--data-and-privacy--storage","content":"Personal Settings > Data and privacy > Storage"},"366":{"id":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference-25","page_id":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference#personal-settings--notifications--telegram","content":"Personal Settings > Notifications > Telegram"},"367":{"id":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference-26","page_id":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference#person-profile--topics-sensitive-subjects","content":"Person profile > Topics (Sensitive subjects)"},"368":{"id":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference-27","page_id":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference#personal-settings--voice","content":"Personal Settings > Voice"},"369":{"id":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference-28","page_id":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference#personal-settings--appearance--appearance","content":"Personal Settings > Appearance > Appearance"},"370":{"id":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference-29","page_id":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference#personal-settings--appearance--ease-of-use","content":"Personal Settings > Appearance > Ease of use"},"371":{"id":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference-30","page_id":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference#robot-settings-1","content":"Robot settings"},"372":{"id":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference-31","page_id":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference#personal-settings--commands-weather","content":"Personal Settings > Commands (weather)"},"373":{"id":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference-32","page_id":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference#this-device","content":"This device"},"374":{"id":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference-33","page_id":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference#robot-hello-this-device","content":"Robot hello (this device)"},"375":{"id":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference-34","page_id":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference","content":"**Home** settings are set once for the household. **Person** settings belong to one person, and the guardian rules decide who may change them for a child or teen. Level is **basic**, **advanced** or **expert**; the app hides higher levels until asked. A blank \"What it does\" means the screen explains it in place. Settings marked \"Not active yet\" are saved but nothing reads them today. Robot and vision settings (keys starting `robot.`, `person.robot.`, `person.vision.` and `vision.`) are used by MaiPai Bot, not by Home itself."},"376":{"id":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference-35","page_id":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference","content":"One more setting, **Wake word listening** (`voice.wakeword.enabled`, device scope, default off), appears only when the wake-word files are installed, so it is not in the tables. Only owners, admins and adults see it. The one detector today is openWakeWord \"Hey Jarvis\", and it runs in the browser. No setup screen downloads the wake-word files; the setting stays hidden until all four are on disk in the `voice/wakewords` data folder (see Where your data lives)."},"377":{"id":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference-36","page_id":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference","content":"Each table gives the label as shown, the key (useful in a support report), the default, the level and what it does. For the same screens in plain language, see the user guide."},"378":{"id":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference-37","page_id":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference#home-settings--engines-and-ai--chat-card","content":"| Setting                        | Key                          | Default | Level    | What it does                                                                                                                                                                         |\n| ------------------------------ | ---------------------------- | ------- | -------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| **Chat context size override** | `chat.context_size_override` | 0       | advanced | 0 lets the hub pick the largest context that fits this computer's memory. A higher number can run out of memory; a lower one leaves headroom but remembers less of the conversation. |","table":"table-0"},"379":{"id":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference-38","page_id":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference#home-settings--engines-and-ai--chat-card","content":"| Setting                      | Key                             | Default | Level    | What it does                                                                                                                                                         |\n| ---------------------------- | ------------------------------- | ------- | -------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| **Flash attention override** | `chat.flash_attention_override` | auto    | advanced | \"Auto\" lets the hub decide based on the model and the quantized-KV-cache setting. Flash attention speeds up longer conversations; a very old GPU may not support it. |","table":"table-0"},"380":{"id":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference-39","page_id":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference#home-settings--engines-and-ai--chat-card","content":"| Setting                         | Key                      | Default | Level    | What it does                                                                                                                                                                                                       |\n| ------------------------------- | ------------------------ | ------- | -------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| **KV cache precision override** | `chat.kv_cache_override` | auto    | advanced | \"Auto\" quantizes the conversation cache to fit more context in the same memory, with a small quality tradeoff. \"Full\" uses full precision: more accurate, uses roughly twice the memory for the same context size. |","table":"table-0"},"381":{"id":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference-40","page_id":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference#home-settings--engines-and-ai--chat-card","content":"| Setting                 | Key             | Default | Level  | What it does                                                                                                  |\n| ----------------------- | --------------- | ------- | ------ | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| **Selected chat model** | `chat.model_id` | empty   | expert | The catalog model id currently downloaded and running for chat. Changed through the AI models page, not here. |","table":"table-0"},"382":{"id":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference-41","page_id":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference#home-settings--engines-and-ai--chat-card","content":"| Setting                              | Key                    | Default  | Level    | What it does                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                            |\n| ------------------------------------ | ---------------------- | -------- | -------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| **How a teen's replies are checked** | `chat.teen_gate_grain` | sentence | advanced | \"Sentence\" checks every sentence before a teen sees it (the default). \"Arrival\" shows a teen's reply as it is written and checks it as it comes, so part of a sentence can show before its check finishes and the reply stops there if the check fails. Children and anything spoken always check every sentence first. |","table":"table-0"},"383":{"id":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference-42","page_id":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference#home-settings--engines-and-ai--chat-card","content":"| Setting               | Key                   | Default | Level | What it does                                                                                             |\n| --------------------- | --------------------- | ------- | ----- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| **Chat model choice** | `engines.chat.choice` | auto    | basic | Choose the model for the Chat role. Auto follows the selected setup plan. Only an admin can change this. |","table":"table-0"},"384":{"id":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference-43","page_id":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference#home-settings--engines-and-ai--chat-card","content":"| Setting                 | Key                     | Default | Level | What it does                                                                                               |\n| ----------------------- | ----------------------- | ------- | ----- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| **Router model choice** | `engines.router.choice` | auto    | basic | Choose the model for the Router role. Auto follows the selected setup plan. Only an admin can change this. |","table":"table-0"},"385":{"id":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference-44","page_id":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference#home-settings--engines-and-ai--chat-card","content":"| Setting                | Key                    | Default | Level | What it does                                                                                              |\n| ---------------------- | ---------------------- | ------- | ----- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| **Embed model choice** | `engines.embed.choice` | auto    | basic | Choose the model for the Embed role. Auto follows the selected setup plan. Only an admin can change this. |","table":"table-0"},"386":{"id":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference-45","page_id":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference#home-settings--engines-and-ai--chat-card","content":"| Setting                 | Key                     | Default | Level | What it does                                                                                               |\n| ----------------------- | ----------------------- | ------- | ----- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| **Rerank model choice** | `engines.rerank.choice` | auto    | basic | Choose the model for the Rerank role. Auto follows the selected setup plan. Only an admin can change this. |","table":"table-0"},"387":{"id":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference-46","page_id":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference#home-settings--engines-and-ai--chat-card","content":"| Setting                 | Key                     | Default | Level | What it does                                                                                               |\n| ----------------------- | ----------------------- | ------- | ----- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| **Vision model choice** | `engines.vision.choice` | auto    | basic | Choose the model for the Vision role. Auto follows the selected setup plan. Only an admin can change this. |","table":"table-0"},"388":{"id":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference-47","page_id":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference#home-settings--engines-and-ai--chat-card","content":"| Setting                | Key                    | Default | Level | What it does                                                                                              |\n| ---------------------- | ---------------------- | ------- | ----- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| **Image model choice** | `engines.image.choice` | auto    | basic | Choose the model for the Image role. Auto follows the selected setup plan. Only an admin can change this. |","table":"table-0"},"389":{"id":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference-48","page_id":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference#home-settings--engines-and-ai--chat-card","content":"| Setting                | Key                    | Default | Level | What it does                                                                                              |\n| ---------------------- | ---------------------- | ------- | ----- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| **Video model choice** | `engines.video.choice` | auto    | basic | Choose the model for the Video role. Auto follows the selected setup plan. Only an admin can change this. |","table":"table-0"},"390":{"id":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference-49","page_id":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference#home-settings--engines-and-ai--chat-card","content":"| Setting                | Key                    | Default | Level | What it does                                                                                              |\n| ---------------------- | ---------------------- | ------- | ----- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| **Music model choice** | `engines.music.choice` | auto    | basic | Choose the model for the Music role. Auto follows the selected setup plan. Only an admin can change this. |","table":"table-0"},"391":{"id":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference-50","page_id":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference#home-settings--engines-and-ai--chat-card","content":"| Setting                 | Key                     | Default | Level | What it does                                                                                               |\n| ----------------------- | ----------------------- | ------- | ----- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| **Coding model choice** | `engines.coding.choice` | auto    | basic | Choose the model for the Coding role. Auto follows the selected setup plan. Only an admin can change this. |","table":"table-0"},"392":{"id":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference-51","page_id":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference#home-settings--engines-and-ai--chat-card","content":"| Setting                | Key                    | Default | Level | What it does                                                                                              |\n| ---------------------- | ---------------------- | ------- | ----- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| **Judge model choice** | `engines.judge.choice` | auto    | basic | Choose the model for the Judge role. Auto follows the selected setup plan. Only an admin can change this. |","table":"table-0"},"393":{"id":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference-52","page_id":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference#home-settings--engines-and-ai--chat-card","content":"| Setting              | Key                  | Default | Level | What it does                                                                                            |\n| -------------------- | -------------------- | ------- | ----- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| **Tts model choice** | `engines.tts.choice` | auto    | basic | Choose the model for the Tts role. Auto follows the selected setup plan. Only an admin can change this. |","table":"table-0"},"394":{"id":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference-53","page_id":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference#home-settings--engines-and-ai--chat-card","content":"| Setting              | Key                  | Default | Level | What it does                                                                                            |\n| -------------------- | -------------------- | ------- | ----- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| **Stt model choice** | `engines.stt.choice` | auto    | basic | Choose the model for the Stt role. Auto follows the selected setup plan. Only an admin can change this. |","table":"table-0"},"395":{"id":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference-54","page_id":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference#home-settings--engines-and-ai--chat-card","content":"| Setting                   | Key                       | Default | Level | What it does                                                                                                 |\n| ------------------------- | ------------------------- | ------- | ----- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| **Wakeword model choice** | `engines.wakeword.choice` | auto    | basic | Choose the model for the Wakeword role. Auto follows the selected setup plan. Only an admin can change this. |","table":"table-0"},"396":{"id":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference-55","page_id":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference#home-settings--engines-and-ai--chat-card","content":"| Setting                      | Key                          | Default | Level | What it does                                                                                                    |\n| ---------------------------- | ---------------------------- | ------- | ----- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| **Turn Signal model choice** | `engines.turn_signal.choice` | auto    | basic | Choose the model for the Turn Signal role. Auto follows the selected setup plan. Only an admin can change this. |","table":"table-0"},"397":{"id":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference-56","page_id":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference#home-settings--engines-and-ai--chat-card","content":"| Setting                                           | Key                                  | Default | Level    | What it does                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                          |\n| ------------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------ | ------- | -------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| **Reach the engine computer when away from home** | `engines.stack.remote.allow_tailnet` | off     | advanced | Off, Home reaches the engine computer only from inside your home network. On, Home may also reach it through your private tailnet when you are away. Turn it on only if you have joined both computers to your tailnet yourself. Only an admin can change this. Shown only while the engine runs on another computer. |","table":"table-0"},"398":{"id":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference-57","page_id":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference#home-settings--engines-and-ai--chat-card","content":"| Setting                  | Key                         | Default | Level | What it does                                                                                                                                                       |\n| ------------------------ | --------------------------- | ------- | ----- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| **Engine computer name** | `engines.stack.remote.host` | empty   | basic | The name of the computer that runs the engine, the way your network knows it. Only an admin can change this. Shown only while the engine runs on another computer. |","table":"table-0"},"399":{"id":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference-58","page_id":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference#home-settings--engines-and-ai--chat-card","content":"| Setting                        | Key                               | Default | Level    | What it does                                                                                                                                                                                                      |\n| ------------------------------ | --------------------------------- | ------- | -------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| **Engine computer local port** | `engines.stack.remote.local_port` | 8771    | advanced | The port on this computer where the engine computer's connection appears. Change it only if another program already uses it. Only an admin can change this. Shown only while the engine runs on another computer. |","table":"table-0"},"400":{"id":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference-59","page_id":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference#home-settings--engines-and-ai--chat-card","content":"| Setting                                    | Key                             | Default | Level    | What it does                                                                                                                                                                                                              |\n| ------------------------------------------ | ------------------------------- | ------- | -------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| **Engine computer secure connection port** | `engines.stack.remote.ssh_port` | 22      | advanced | The port Home uses to open its secure connection to the engine computer. Leave it at 22 unless that computer was set up differently. Only an admin can change this. Shown only while the engine runs on another computer. |","table":"table-0"},"401":{"id":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference-60","page_id":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference#home-settings--engines-and-ai--chat-card","content":"| Setting                  | Key                 | Default | Level  | What it does                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                         |\n| ------------------------ | ------------------- | ------- | ------ | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| **MaiPai Stack address** | `engines.stack.url` | empty   | expert | Empty uses Home's own built-in engines. With the engine on this computer, set this to the address of the MaiPai Stack installed here to route chat, embeddings and voice through it. With the engine on another computer, Home fills this in for you from the connection settings, so leave it empty. Only an admin can change this. |","table":"table-0"},"402":{"id":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference-61","page_id":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference#home-settings--engines-and-ai--chat-card","content":"| Setting                                      | Key                  | Default | Level    | What it does                                                                                                                                                                                                                                               |\n| -------------------------------------------- | -------------------- | ------- | -------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| **Help the chat remember to search the web** | `chat.search_assist` | shadow  | advanced | \"Off\" is the kill switch: nothing is scored. \"Shadow\" (the default) only counts, as a number, how often a web search looked needed, and changes no reply. \"Rescue\" is not active yet; for now it behaves like shadow. Children and teens are never scored. |","table":"table-0"},"403":{"id":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference-62","page_id":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference#home-settings--engines-and-ai--chat-card","content":"| Setting                           | Key                      | Default | Level  | What it does                                               |\n| --------------------------------- | ------------------------ | ------- | ------ | ---------------------------------------------------------- |\n| **Use the MaiPai Stack for chat** | `engines.stack.use_chat` | off     | expert | Deprecated, ignored. A configured Stack serves every role. |","table":"table-0"},"404":{"id":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference-63","page_id":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference#home-settings--engines-and-ai--chat-card","content":"| Setting                                          | Key                            | Default | Level  | What it does                                               |\n| ------------------------------------------------ | ------------------------------ | ------- | ------ | ---------------------------------------------------------- |\n| **Use the MaiPai Stack for search (embeddings)** | `engines.stack.use_embeddings` | off     | expert | Deprecated, ignored. A configured Stack serves every role. |","table":"table-0"},"405":{"id":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference-64","page_id":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference#home-settings--engines-and-ai--chat-card","content":"| Setting                                                 | Key                     | Default | Level  | What it does                                               |\n| ------------------------------------------------------- | ----------------------- | ------- | ------ | ---------------------------------------------------------- |\n| **Use the MaiPai Stack for listening (speech to text)** | `engines.stack.use_stt` | off     | expert | Deprecated, ignored. A configured Stack serves every role. |","table":"table-0"},"406":{"id":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference-65","page_id":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference#home-settings--engines-and-ai--chat-card","content":"| Setting                                                | Key                     | Default | Level  | What it does                                               |\n| ------------------------------------------------------ | ----------------------- | ------- | ------ | ---------------------------------------------------------- |\n| **Use the MaiPai Stack for speaking (text to speech)** | `engines.stack.use_tts` | off     | expert | Deprecated, ignored. A configured Stack serves every role. |","table":"table-0"},"407":{"id":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference-66","page_id":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference#home-settings--engines-and-ai--chat-card","content":"| Setting                   | Key                   | Default       | Level | What it does                                                                                                                                                                                          |\n| ------------------------- | --------------------- | ------------- | ----- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| **Where the engine runs** | `engines.stack.where` | this_computer | basic | \"This computer\" runs the engine on the machine Home is installed on. \"Another computer\" runs it on a different computer in your home that you reach over your network. Only an admin can change this. |","table":"table-0"},"408":{"id":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference-67","page_id":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference#home-settings--engines-and-ai--chat-card","content":"| Setting                                    | Key              | Default | Level    | What it does                                                                                                                                                                  |\n| ------------------------------------------ | ---------------- | ------- | -------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| **Hugging Face token (for voice cloning)** | `voice.hf_token` | empty   | advanced | Needed to clone a voice from a recording. Accept the terms at huggingface.co/kyutai/pocket-tts, then create a read token at huggingface.co/settings/tokens and paste it here. |","table":"table-0"},"409":{"id":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference-68","page_id":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference#home-settings--search--blocked-sites","content":"| Setting                               | Key                       | Default                                  | Level    | What it does                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                            |\n| ------------------------------------- | ------------------------- | ---------------------------------------- | -------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| **Blocked sites with child controls** | `search.blocklists.child` | [\"blp-gambling\", \"blp-scam\", \"blp-phishi | advanced | Which lists of blocked sites are checked when MaiPai searches the web for people using child controls. Adult sites are always blocked for child and teen controls and are not listed here. Home downloads each list once and keeps it up to date. Web search for child controls starts once every list checked here has been downloaded. Only an admin can change this. |","table":"table-1"},"410":{"id":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference-69","page_id":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference#home-settings--search--blocked-sites","content":"| Setting                              | Key                      | Default                                  | Level    | What it does                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                 |\n| ------------------------------------ | ------------------------ | ---------------------------------------- | -------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| **Blocked sites with teen controls** | `search.blocklists.teen` | [\"blp-gambling\", \"blp-scam\", \"blp-phishi | advanced | Which lists of blocked sites are checked when MaiPai searches the web for people using teen controls. Adult sites are always blocked for child and teen controls and are not listed here. Web search for teen controls starts once every list checked here has been downloaded. Only an admin can change this. It does not show anyone what a teen searched for or which sites were blocked. |","table":"table-1"},"411":{"id":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference-70","page_id":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference#home-settings--search--blocked-sites","content":"| Setting                               | Key                       | Default | Level    | What it does                                                                                                                                                                                                                                 |\n| ------------------------------------- | ------------------------- | ------- | -------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| **Blocked sites with adult controls** | `search.blocklists.adult` | []      | advanced | Lists of blocked sites to check when MaiPai searches the web for adults. None are checked unless you pick them. Scam, phishing and malware lists are a good start for a household that wants that protection. Only an admin can change this. |","table":"table-1"},"412":{"id":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference-71","page_id":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference#home-settings--search--blocked-sites","content":"| Setting                     | Key                 | Default | Level    | What it does                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                      |\n| --------------------------- | ------------------- | ------- | -------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| **Kinds of sites to block** | `search.blocklists` | []      | advanced | Kinds of sites that web search, page reads and answer pictures leave out. Kids, Teens and Adults each start from their own user defaults. The global defaults add kinds for everyone, and a user override adds or removes kinds for one person. The adult-site list is always on for a child or teen and no override can turn it off. Only an admin can change this, and it never shows what anyone searched for. |","table":"table-1"},"413":{"id":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference-72","page_id":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference#home-settings--search--blocked-sites","content":"| Setting                      | Key                 | Default | Level    | What it does                                                                                                                                                                                                                           |\n| ---------------------------- | ------------------- | ------- | -------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| **Always block these sites** | `search.hosts.deny` | empty   | advanced | Sites that web search never shows for anyone, separated by commas, like example.com. A site you list here also blocks its subpages. This works for every age, and it always wins over the allowed list. Only an admin can change this. |","table":"table-1"},"414":{"id":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference-73","page_id":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference#home-settings--search--blocked-sites","content":"| Setting               | Key                  | Default | Level    | What it does                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                |\n| --------------------- | -------------------- | ------- | -------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| **Allow these sites** | `search.hosts.allow` | empty   | advanced | Sites that web search may show even when a blocked-sites list has them, separated by commas, like example.com. It cannot allow an adult site for child or teen controls, and it cannot allow a site you list under Always block these sites. Only an admin can change this. |","table":"table-1"},"415":{"id":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference-74","page_id":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference#home-settings--search--blocked-sites","content":"| Setting                                | Key                       | Default | Level    | What it does                                                                                                                                                                                                                            |\n| -------------------------------------- | ------------------------- | ------- | -------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| **Always block these sites for child** | `search.hosts.child.deny` | empty   | advanced | Sites that web search never shows to a child, separated by commas, like example.com, on top of the household list. A site you list here also blocks its subpages. It always wins over the allowed lists. Only an admin can change this. |","table":"table-1"},"416":{"id":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference-75","page_id":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference#home-settings--search--blocked-sites","content":"| Setting                         | Key                        | Default | Level    | What it does                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                 |\n| ------------------------------- | -------------------------- | ------- | -------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| **Allow these sites for child** | `search.hosts.child.allow` | empty   | advanced | Sites that web search may show to a child even when a blocked-sites list has them, separated by commas, like example.com, on top of the household list. It cannot allow an adult site for child or teen controls, and it cannot allow a site that is in an always-block list. Only an admin can change this. |","table":"table-1"},"417":{"id":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference-76","page_id":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference#home-settings--search--blocked-sites","content":"| Setting                               | Key                      | Default | Level    | What it does                                                                                                                                                                                                                           |\n| ------------------------------------- | ------------------------ | ------- | -------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| **Always block these sites for teen** | `search.hosts.teen.deny` | empty   | advanced | Sites that web search never shows to a teen, separated by commas, like example.com, on top of the household list. A site you list here also blocks its subpages. It always wins over the allowed lists. Only an admin can change this. |","table":"table-1"},"418":{"id":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference-77","page_id":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference#home-settings--search--blocked-sites","content":"| Setting                        | Key                       | Default | Level    | What it does                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                |\n| ------------------------------ | ------------------------- | ------- | -------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| **Allow these sites for teen** | `search.hosts.teen.allow` | empty   | advanced | Sites that web search may show to a teen even when a blocked-sites list has them, separated by commas, like example.com, on top of the household list. It cannot allow an adult site for child or teen controls, and it cannot allow a site that is in an always-block list. Only an admin can change this. |","table":"table-1"},"419":{"id":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference-78","page_id":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference#home-settings--search--blocked-sites","content":"| Setting                                | Key                       | Default | Level    | What it does                                                                                                                                                                                                                             |\n| -------------------------------------- | ------------------------- | ------- | -------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| **Always block these sites for adult** | `search.hosts.adult.deny` | empty   | advanced | Sites that web search never shows to an adult, separated by commas, like example.com, on top of the household list. A site you list here also blocks its subpages. It always wins over the allowed lists. Only an admin can change this. |","table":"table-1"},"420":{"id":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference-79","page_id":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference#home-settings--search--blocked-sites","content":"| Setting                         | Key                        | Default | Level    | What it does                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                  |\n| ------------------------------- | -------------------------- | ------- | -------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| **Allow these sites for adult** | `search.hosts.adult.allow` | empty   | advanced | Sites that web search may show to an adult even when a blocked-sites list has them, separated by commas, like example.com, on top of the household list. It cannot allow an adult site for child or teen controls, and it cannot allow a site that is in an always-block list. Only an admin can change this. |","table":"table-1"},"421":{"id":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference-80","page_id":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference#home-settings--integrations--home-assistant","content":"| Setting                         | Key                 | Default | Level    | What it does                                                                                              |\n| ------------------------------- | ------------------- | ------- | -------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| **Home Assistant access token** | `home.access_token` | empty   | advanced | A long-lived access token from your Home Assistant profile page, used to control your smart-home devices. |","table":"table-2"},"422":{"id":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference-81","page_id":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference#home-settings--integrations--home-assistant","content":"| Setting                | Key             | Default | Level    | What it does                                                                       |\n| ---------------------- | --------------- | ------- | -------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| **Home Assistant URL** | `home.base_url` | empty   | advanced | The address of your Home Assistant instance, e.g. http://homeassistant.local:8123. |","table":"table-2"},"423":{"id":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference-82","page_id":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference#home-settings--integrations--home-assistant","content":"| Setting                  | Key                    | Default | Level | What it does                                                                                       |\n| ------------------------ | ---------------------- | ------- | ----- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| **Safety alarm sensors** | `safety.alarm.sensors` | []      | basic | Home Assistant sensors whose alarm events the robot announces. No sensors are selected by default. |","table":"table-2"},"424":{"id":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference-83","page_id":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference#home-settings--network-and-access--network","content":"| Setting               | Key                | Default | Level  | What it does                                                                                                              |\n| --------------------- | ------------------ | ------- | ------ | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| **Home network port** | `network.hub_port` | 3000    | expert | The port Home listens on. Changing it needs a restart and changes the address devices use. Only an admin can change this. |","table":"table-3"},"425":{"id":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference-84","page_id":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference#home-settings--network-and-access--network","content":"| Setting                | Key                    | Default | Level    | What it does                                                                                                                                       |\n| ---------------------- | ---------------------- | ------- | -------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| **Who can reach Home** | `network.lan_exposure` | lan     | advanced | Loopback keeps Home on this computer. LAN lets devices on your home network connect. Changing this needs a restart. Only an admin can change this. |","table":"table-3"},"426":{"id":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference-85","page_id":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference#home-settings--network-and-access--network","content":"| Setting                           | Key                      | Default | Level | What it does                                                                                                                                                                                             |\n| --------------------------------- | ------------------------ | ------- | ----- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| **Away access through Tailscale** | `network.tailnet_access` | off     | basic | Lets your devices reach Home through your private Tailscale network. Tailscale sees device names and addresses, not your conversations. Home never turns this on for you. Only an admin can change this. |","table":"table-3"},"427":{"id":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference-86","page_id":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference#home-settings--search--news-shelf","content":"| Setting                          | Key                    | Default | Level    | What it does                                                    |\n| -------------------------------- | ---------------------- | ------- | -------- | --------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| **News poll interval (seconds)** | `news.poll_interval_s` | 1800    | advanced | How often Home checks enabled news feeds. At least 900 seconds. |","table":"table-4"},"428":{"id":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference-87","page_id":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference#home-settings--search--news-shelf","content":"| Setting                   | Key                   | Default | Level    | What it does                                |\n| ------------------------- | --------------------- | ------- | -------- | ------------------------------------------- |\n| **News retention (days)** | `news.retention_days` | 90      | advanced | How long Home keeps news items and stories. |","table":"table-4"},"429":{"id":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference-88","page_id":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference#home-settings--search--news-shelf","content":"| Setting        | Key                  | Default | Level    | What it does                             |\n| -------------- | -------------------- | ------- | -------- | ---------------------------------------- |\n| **News shelf** | `news.shelf.enabled` | on      | advanced | Turn the household news shelf on or off. |","table":"table-4"},"430":{"id":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference-89","page_id":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference#home-settings--search--news-shelf","content":"| Setting                            | Key                | Default            | Level | What it does                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                              |\n| ---------------------------------- | ------------------ | ------------------ | ----- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| **News lists with child controls** | `news.lists.child` | [\"feeds-children\"] | basic | Which lists of news feeds appear on the news shelf for people using child controls. A list that is not offered to this user type never appears here and is never shown to them. Every item is still checked by the age filter before anyone sees it. A list unchecked for every user type is switched off. Only an admin can change this. |","table":"table-4"},"431":{"id":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference-90","page_id":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference#home-settings--search--news-shelf","content":"| Setting                           | Key               | Default             | Level | What it does                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                             |\n| --------------------------------- | ----------------- | ------------------- | ----- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| **News lists with teen controls** | `news.lists.teen` | [\"feeds-household\"] | basic | Which lists of news feeds appear on the news shelf for people using teen controls. A list that is not offered to this user type never appears here and is never shown to them. Every item is still checked by the age filter before anyone sees it. A list unchecked for every user type is switched off. Only an admin can change this. |","table":"table-4"},"432":{"id":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference-91","page_id":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference#home-settings--search--news-shelf","content":"| Setting                            | Key                | Default             | Level | What it does                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                              |\n| ---------------------------------- | ------------------ | ------------------- | ----- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| **News lists with adult controls** | `news.lists.adult` | [\"feeds-household\"] | basic | Which lists of news feeds appear on the news shelf for people using adult controls. A list that is not offered to this user type never appears here and is never shown to them. Every item is still checked by the age filter before anyone sees it. A list unchecked for every user type is switched off. Only an admin can change this. |","table":"table-4"},"433":{"id":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference-92","page_id":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference#home-settings--search--news-shelf","content":"| Setting                        | Key                | Default | Level    | What it does                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                     |\n| ------------------------------ | ------------------ | ------- | -------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| **Extra news feeds for child** | `news.feeds.child` | empty   | advanced | News feed addresses to add for people using child controls, starting with https:// and separated by commas or spaces. Remove an address to remove its feed. These sit on top of the checked lists. Home checks every item against the age filter, and an address that points inside your home network is refused. Only an admin can change this. |","table":"table-4"},"434":{"id":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference-93","page_id":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference#home-settings--search--news-shelf","content":"| Setting                       | Key               | Default | Level    | What it does                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                    |\n| ----------------------------- | ----------------- | ------- | -------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| **Extra news feeds for teen** | `news.feeds.teen` | empty   | advanced | News feed addresses to add for people using teen controls, starting with https:// and separated by commas or spaces. Remove an address to remove its feed. These sit on top of the checked lists. Home checks every item against the age filter, and an address that points inside your home network is refused. Only an admin can change this. |","table":"table-4"},"435":{"id":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference-94","page_id":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference#home-settings--search--news-shelf","content":"| Setting                        | Key                | Default | Level    | What it does                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                     |\n| ------------------------------ | ------------------ | ------- | -------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| **Extra news feeds for adult** | `news.feeds.adult` | empty   | advanced | News feed addresses to add for people using adult controls, starting with https:// and separated by commas or spaces. Remove an address to remove its feed. These sit on top of the checked lists. Home checks every item against the age filter, and an address that points inside your home network is refused. Only an admin can change this. |","table":"table-4"},"436":{"id":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference-95","page_id":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference#home-settings--integrations--telegram","content":"| Setting               | Key                          | Default | Level | What it does                                                                        |\n| --------------------- | ---------------------------- | ------- | ----- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| **Quiet hours start** | `household.quiet_hours.from` | 21:00   | basic | Quiet hours begin at 9:00 pm by default. Safety alarms always override quiet hours. |","table":"table-5"},"437":{"id":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference-96","page_id":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference#home-settings--integrations--telegram","content":"| Setting             | Key                        | Default | Level | What it does                           |\n| ------------------- | -------------------------- | ------- | ----- | -------------------------------------- |\n| **Quiet hours end** | `household.quiet_hours.to` | 07:00   | basic | Quiet hours end at 7:00 am by default. |","table":"table-5"},"438":{"id":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference-97","page_id":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference#home-settings--integrations--telegram","content":"| Setting                | Key                                | Default | Level    | What it does                                                                                                                                  |\n| ---------------------- | ---------------------------------- | ------- | -------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| **Telegram bot token** | `notifications.telegram.bot_token` | empty   | advanced | A bot token from @BotFather, used to send notifications to Telegram. One bot for the whole household; each person links their own chat below. |","table":"table-5"},"439":{"id":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference-98","page_id":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference#home-settings--integrations--reference-library","content":"| Setting                        | Key                     | Default | Level | What it does                                                                                                                                                                                                    |\n| ------------------------------ | ----------------------- | ------- | ----- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| **Reference library location** | `reference.library_dir` | empty   | basic | Where the household's offline knowledge archives live: a local folder, an external drive, or a NAS mount. Empty uses Home's own data folder. Moving this later moves the files and updates the library records. |","table":"table-6"},"440":{"id":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference-99","page_id":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference#home-settings--integrations--reference-library","content":"| Setting                                 | Key                         | Default | Level    | What it does                                               |\n| --------------------------------------- | --------------------------- | ------- | -------- | ---------------------------------------------------------- |\n| **Reference update speed limit (MB/s)** | `reference.update.max_mbps` | 20      | advanced | Not active yet. Planned; this setting has no effect today. |","table":"table-6"},"441":{"id":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference-100","page_id":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference#home-settings--search--web-search","content":"| Setting                  | Key                          | Default | Level    | What it does                                                                                                                                    |\n| ------------------------ | ---------------------------- | ------- | -------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| **Look up words online** | `search.dictionary_fallback` | off     | advanced | Look up a word online when the library does not have it. The word you ask about is sent to Wiktionary (Wikimedia). Adults only. Off by default. |","table":"table-7"},"442":{"id":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference-101","page_id":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference#home-settings--search--web-search","content":"| Setting                           | Key                     | Default | Level    | What it does                                                                                           |\n| --------------------------------- | ----------------------- | ------- | -------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| **Search fetch cache limit (GB)** | `search.fetch_cache_gb` | 2       | advanced | Maximum disk space used for cached search pages. The default is 2 GB on p16 and 10 GB on p64 and p128. |","table":"table-7"},"443":{"id":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference-102","page_id":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference#home-settings--search--web-search","content":"| Setting                         | Key                  | Default | Level    | What it does                                                                            |\n| ------------------------------- | -------------------- | ------- | -------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| **Your own SearXNG (optional)** | `search.searxng_url` | empty   | advanced | Your own SearXNG (optional). Leave empty to use the search service MaiPai runs for you. |","table":"table-7"},"444":{"id":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference-103","page_id":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference#home-settings--search--web-search","content":"| Setting            | Key                  | Default | Level | What it does                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                  |\n| ------------------ | -------------------- | ------- | ----- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| **Search sources** | `search.source_mode` | mix     | basic | Where MaiPai looks for answers: Internet first, Library only, or Library first (the recommended choice). Library only turns off just the live Wikipedia-style lookup; web search stays on unless web search is itself set to Library only. Children and teens keep their current protections in every mode, and this choice never widens what they can reach. |","table":"table-7"},"445":{"id":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference-104","page_id":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference#home-settings--search--web-search","content":"| Setting                  | Key                            | Default | Level    | What it does                                                                                                                                                                                                     |\n| ------------------------ | ------------------------------ | ------- | -------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| **Encyclopedia lookups** | `search.source_mode.wikimedia` | inherit | advanced | Gives the live Wikipedia-style lookup its own choice. Same as the household choice follows the search sources setting. Library only turns this lookup off. Children and teens never use this lookup in any mode. |","table":"table-7"},"446":{"id":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference-105","page_id":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference#home-settings--search--web-search","content":"| Setting          | Key                      | Default | Level    | What it does                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                              |\n| ---------------- | ------------------------ | ------- | -------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| **Web searches** | `search.source_mode.web` | inherit | advanced | Gives web search its own choice. Same as the household choice follows the search sources setting. Library only here turns off web search, link reading, Wayback and the hosted search provider together. Children and teens keep their current protections in every mode. |","table":"table-7"},"447":{"id":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference-106","page_id":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference#home-settings--search--web-search","content":"| Setting                            | Key                     | Default | Level | What it does                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                            |\n| ---------------------------------- | ----------------------- | ------- | ----- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| **Web search with child controls** | `search.web.child_mode` | on      | basic | When this is on, MaiPai can look things up on the web for people using child controls. Results go through SafeSearch at its strictest, adult sites are blocked, and links are hidden. When it is off, answers come only from the offline library. Only an admin can change this, and a child's searches show in that child's own chats. |","table":"table-7"},"448":{"id":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference-107","page_id":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference#home-settings--search--web-search","content":"| Setting                           | Key                    | Default | Level | What it does                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                           |\n| --------------------------------- | ---------------------- | ------- | ----- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| **Web search with teen controls** | `search.web.teen_mode` | on      | basic | When this is on, MaiPai can look things up on the web for people using teen controls. Results go through SafeSearch at moderate or stricter, and adult sites are blocked. When it is off, answers come only from the offline library. Only an admin can change this. It does not show anyone what a teen searched for. |","table":"table-7"},"449":{"id":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference-108","page_id":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference#home-settings--search--web-search","content":"| Setting                | Key                  | Default     | Level    | What it does                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                   |\n| ---------------------- | -------------------- | ----------- | -------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| **Web search sources** | `search.web_sources` | [\"searxng\"] | advanced | Which services answer web searches. SearXNG, the household's own search service, is on by default. DuckDuckGo is not available yet. With more than one picked, their results are blended into one list. Children and teens only use SearXNG. To turn web search off, set Web searches to Library only. Pictures and videos always use SearXNG. |","table":"table-7"},"450":{"id":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference-109","page_id":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference#home-settings--search--web-search","content":"| Setting                                         | Key                       | Default | Level    | What it does                                                   |\n| ----------------------------------------------- | ------------------------- | ------- | -------- | -------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| **Use archived pages when a source is missing** | `search.wayback_fallback` | on      | advanced | Check the Wayback Machine when a cited page returns not found. |","table":"table-7"},"451":{"id":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference-110","page_id":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference#home-settings--search--web-search","content":"| Setting                         | Key                    | Default | Level    | What it does                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                             |\n| ------------------------------- | ---------------------- | ------- | -------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| **Brave Search key (optional)** | `search.brave_api_key` | empty   | advanced | Optional. Search works without any key. If you add a Brave Search API key, an adult's web searches go to Brave Search instead of your SearXNG, so the words searched leave your house. A child's or teen's searches never do. The key is stored encrypted and can't be read back. Clear it to go back to keyless search. |","table":"table-7"},"452":{"id":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference-111","page_id":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference#home-settings--general--internet-check","content":"| Setting                 | Key                              | Default     | Level    | What it does                                                                        |\n| ----------------------- | -------------------------------- | ----------- | -------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| **Internet check name** | `status.internet_probe.dns_name` | example.com | advanced | The name MaiPai looks up once a minute to check whether internet name lookups work. |","table":"table-8"},"453":{"id":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference-112","page_id":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference#home-settings--general--internet-check","content":"| Setting                                     | Key                             | Default | Level | What it does                                                                                                                           |\n| ------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------- | ------- | ----- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| **Check whether the internet is reachable** | `status.internet_probe.enabled` | on      | basic | Once a minute, MaiPai looks up a neutral name and opens an empty connection to the chosen address. Turn this off to stop those checks. |","table":"table-8"},"454":{"id":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference-113","page_id":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference#home-settings--general--internet-check","content":"| Setting                    | Key                                 | Default | Level    | What it does                                                                 |\n| -------------------------- | ----------------------------------- | ------- | -------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| **Internet check address** | `status.internet_probe.tcp_address` | 1.1.1.1 | advanced | The public IP address MaiPai connects to once a minute without sending data. |","table":"table-8"},"455":{"id":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference-114","page_id":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference#home-settings--general--internet-check","content":"| Setting                 | Key                              | Default | Level    | What it does                                                       |\n| ----------------------- | -------------------------------- | ------- | -------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| **Internet check port** | `status.internet_probe.tcp_port` | 443     | advanced | The port MaiPai opens and immediately closes without sending data. |","table":"table-8"},"456":{"id":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference-115","page_id":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference#home-settings--storage-and-backups--limits","content":"| Setting                       | Key                   | Default | Level    | What it does                                                                                                                                                                   |\n| ----------------------------- | --------------------- | ------- | -------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| **Backup storage limit (GB)** | `backup.max_total_gb` | 0       | advanced | Once total backup storage passes this, the oldest backups are deleted first - checked after the normal seven-daily/four-weekly/three-monthly schedule. 0 means no extra limit. |","table":"table-9"},"457":{"id":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference-116","page_id":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference#home-settings--storage-and-backups--limits","content":"| Setting              | Key                              | Default | Level | What it does                                                                                                |\n| -------------------- | -------------------------------- | ------- | ----- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| **Backup key saved** | `backups.emergency_kit_saved_at` | empty   | basic | The date and time the owner saved or printed the emergency backup key. The key itself is never stored here. |","table":"table-9"},"458":{"id":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference-117","page_id":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference#home-settings--storage-and-backups--limits","content":"| Setting                                        | Key                        | Default | Level    | What it does                                                                     |\n| ---------------------------------------------- | -------------------------- | ------- | -------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| **Warn when free disk space drops below (GB)** | `storage.critical_free_gb` | 2       | advanced | A Repairs item is raised once free space on the hub's own disk drops below this. |","table":"table-9"},"459":{"id":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference-118","page_id":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference#home-settings--storage-and-backups--limits","content":"| Setting                           | Key                           | Default | Level | What it does                                                                                                               |\n| --------------------------------- | ----------------------------- | ------- | ----- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| **Household storage cap (bytes)** | `storage.household.cap_bytes` | 0       | basic | The total bytes the whole household's files may use. 0 means no cap is set yet - the setup wizard sets this from the disk. |","table":"table-9"},"460":{"id":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference-119","page_id":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference#home-settings--storage-and-backups--limits","content":"| Setting                                    | Key                                | Default     | Level | What it does                                                                                             |\n| ------------------------------------------ | ---------------------------------- | ----------- | ----- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| **Default per-person storage cap (bytes)** | `storage.person.default_cap_bytes` | 21474836480 | basic | How many bytes each person may use for their own files, unless that person has their own override below. |","table":"table-9"},"461":{"id":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference-120","page_id":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference#home-settings--general--household","content":"| Setting                            | Key                                     | Default | Level    | What it does                                                                                                                                                               |\n| ---------------------------------- | --------------------------------------- | ------- | -------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| **Conversation history retention** | `household.conversation_retention_days` | 90      | advanced | How long chat history is kept before it's deleted. A safety-flagged conversation involving a teen or child is always kept for at least 90 days regardless of this setting. |","table":"table-10"},"462":{"id":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference-121","page_id":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference#home-settings--general--household","content":"| Setting         | Key                     | Default | Level | What it does                                                     |\n| --------------- | ----------------------- | ------- | ----- | ---------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| **Family name** | `household.family_name` | empty   | basic | Not active yet. The name is saved but Home does not show it yet. |","table":"table-10"},"463":{"id":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference-122","page_id":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference#home-settings--general--household","content":"| Setting           | Key              | Default | Level | What it does                                                         |\n| ----------------- | ---------------- | ------- | ----- | -------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| **Home location** | `household.home` | empty   | basic | The household place used as the fallback for location-based answers. |","table":"table-10"},"464":{"id":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference-123","page_id":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference#home-settings--general--household","content":"| Setting                 | Key                | Default | Level | What it does                                          |\n| ----------------------- | ------------------ | ------- | ----- | ----------------------------------------------------- |\n| **Language and region** | `household.locale` | en-US   | basic | Sets the household's date, time, and unit formatting. |","table":"table-10"},"465":{"id":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference-124","page_id":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference#home-settings--general--household","content":"| Setting                | Key                    | Default | Level | What it does                                     |\n| ---------------------- | ---------------------- | ------- | ----- | ------------------------------------------------ |\n| **Household location** | `household.home_place` | empty   | basic | The place MaiPai uses as the household fallback. |","table":"table-10"},"466":{"id":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference-125","page_id":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference#home-settings--privacy--sensitive-subjects","content":"| Setting                                         | Key                  | Default     | Level | What it does                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                    |\n| ----------------------------------------------- | -------------------- | ----------- | ----- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| **Bodies and relationships with teen controls** | `topics.teen.bodies` | informative | basic | How MaiPai answers teens' questions about puberty, sex, consent, relationships and identity. The standard answer is factual and respectful, and never sexual or romantic. It applies to everyone on teen controls and is set by an admin. An admin cannot see what a teen asks. |","table":"table-11"},"467":{"id":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference-126","page_id":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference#home-settings--privacy--sensitive-subjects","content":"| Setting                                           | Key                | Default     | Level | What it does                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                               |\n| ------------------------------------------------- | ------------------ | ----------- | ----- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| **Drugs, alcohol and betting with teen controls** | `topics.teen.risk` | informative | basic | How MaiPai answers teens' questions about drugs, alcohol, vaping, gambling and dangerous challenges. The standard answer explains the real risks and how to get help fast, and never gives tips for getting high, buying or betting. It applies to everyone on teen controls and is set by an admin. An admin cannot see what a teen asks. |","table":"table-11"},"468":{"id":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference-127","page_id":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference#robot-settings","content":"| Setting                  | Key                    | Default | Level | What it does                                                                            |\n| ------------------------ | ---------------------- | ------- | ----- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| **Robot greeting style** | `robot.greetings.mode` | gesture | basic | Use a gesture by default; spoken greeting remains subject to person and age-band rules. |","table":"table-12"},"469":{"id":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference-128","page_id":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference#robot-settings","content":"| Setting                      | Key                               | Default | Level | What it does                                                                                                                             |\n| ---------------------------- | --------------------------------- | ------- | ----- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| **Offer acceptance phrases** | `robot.initiative.accept_phrases` | default | basic | Uses the closed default set: “go ahead” or “yes please” to accept, and “not now” or “no thanks” to decline. No gesture accepts an offer. |","table":"table-12"},"470":{"id":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference-129","page_id":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference#robot-settings","content":"| Setting              | Key                        | Default | Level | What it does                                                                                                                   |\n| -------------------- | -------------------------- | ------- | ----- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| **Robot initiative** | `robot.initiative.enabled` | on      | basic | When on, the robot may make approved offers. On by default for gestures only; spoken offers remain controlled by tiers_spoken. |","table":"table-12"},"471":{"id":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference-130","page_id":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference#robot-settings","content":"| Setting                     | Key                                    | Default | Level | What it does                                                        |\n| --------------------------- | -------------------------------------- | ------- | ----- | ------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| **Maximum offers per hour** | `robot.initiative.max_offers_per_hour` | 3       | basic | At most three offers per hour by default; tier 3 is limited to one. |","table":"table-12"},"472":{"id":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference-131","page_id":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference#robot-settings","content":"| Setting                | Key                             | Default | Level | What it does                                          |\n| ---------------------- | ------------------------------- | ------- | ----- | ----------------------------------------------------- |\n| **Spoken offer tiers** | `robot.initiative.tiers_spoken` | tier_1  | basic | Tier 1 may speak; tiers 2 and 3 ask first by default. |","table":"table-12"},"473":{"id":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference-132","page_id":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference#robot-settings","content":"| Setting                   | Key                       | Default | Level | What it does                                                                                            |\n| ------------------------- | ------------------------- | ------- | ----- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| **Allow robot live view** | `robot.live_view.enabled` | off     | basic | Off until an admin enables it. Only admins and adults explicitly named in robot.live_view.who may view. |","table":"table-12"},"474":{"id":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference-133","page_id":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference#robot-settings","content":"| Setting                                     | Key                   | Default | Level | What it does                                                                            |\n| ------------------------------------------- | --------------------- | ------- | ----- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| **Adults allowed to view the robot camera** | `robot.live_view.who` | []      | basic | Admins can view. This list may name adults only; children and teens are never admitted. |","table":"table-12"},"475":{"id":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference-134","page_id":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference#robot-settings","content":"| Setting                                 | Key                    | Default | Level    | What it does                                                                                                                |\n| --------------------------------------- | ---------------------- | ------- | -------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| **Allow robot access over the tailnet** | `robot.offlan.tailnet` | off     | advanced | Off by default. Turn on only after the owner manually joins the device to the household tailnet; Home holds no tailnet key. |","table":"table-12"},"476":{"id":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference-135","page_id":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference#robot-settings","content":"| Setting                     | Key                       | Default                                  | Level | What it does                                    |\n| --------------------------- | ------------------------- | ---------------------------------------- | ----- | ----------------------------------------------- |\n| **Child safety alarm line** | `safety.alarm.child_line` | Smoke alarm. Please go to your grown-up. | basic | Spoken after a mapped safety alarm for a child. |","table":"table-12"},"477":{"id":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference-136","page_id":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference#robot-settings","content":"| Setting                          | Key                           | Default | Level | What it does                                             |\n| -------------------------------- | ----------------------------- | ------- | ----- | -------------------------------------------------------- |\n| **Safety alarm repeat interval** | `safety.alarm.repeat_seconds` | 20      | basic | Repeat between 10 and 60 seconds; 20 seconds by default. |","table":"table-12"},"478":{"id":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference-137","page_id":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference#robot-settings","content":"| Setting                | Key                  | Default | Level | What it does                                                              |\n| ---------------------- | -------------------- | ------- | ----- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| **Safety alarm voice** | `safety.alarm.voice` | default | basic | The fixed alarm voice; the deterministic alarm path does not use a model. |","table":"table-12"},"479":{"id":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference-138","page_id":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference#robot-settings","content":"| Setting                 | Key                   | Default | Level | What it does                                                  |\n| ----------------------- | --------------------- | --