                          | Default | Level | What it does                                                                                                       |\n| ------------------------- | -------------------------------- | ------- | ----- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| **Your Telegram chat id** | `notifications.telegram.chat_id` | empty   | basic | Message the household bot once, then paste the chat id it replies with, to receive your notifications on Telegram. |","table":"table-22"},"523":{"id":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference-182","page_id":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference#personal-settings--notifications--telegram","content":"| Setting                                                | Key                                        | Default | Level | What it does |\n| ------------------------------------------------------ | ------------------------------------------ | ------- | ----- | ------------ |\n| **Telegram me when a MaiPai Home update is available** | `notifications.updates.available.telegram` | off     | basic |              |","table":"table-22"},"524":{"id":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference-183","page_id":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference#person-profile--topics-sensitive-subjects","content":"| Setting                      | Key             | Default | Level | What it does                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                          |\n| ---------------------------- | --------------- | ------- | ----- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| **Bodies and relationships** | `topics.bodies` | default | basic | How MaiPai answers a child's questions about bodies, babies, crushes and relationships. The standard answer gently points them to you. Only a parent or admin can change a child's. It applies only while the person is on child controls and never reaches the care, safety and fairness rules, which stay the same for every child. |","table":"table-23"},"525":{"id":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference-184","page_id":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference#person-profile--topics-sensitive-subjects","content":"| Setting                       | Key             | Default | Level | What it does                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                     |\n| ----------------------------- | --------------- | ------- | ----- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| **Illness, death and health** | `topics.health` | default | basic | How MaiPai answers a child's questions about illness, death, grief and medicine. The standard answer is honest, short and gentle. Only a parent or admin can change a child's. It applies only while the person is on child controls and never reaches the care, safety and fairness rules, which stay the same for every child. |","table":"table-23"},"526":{"id":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference-185","page_id":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference#person-profile--topics-sensitive-subjects","content":"| Setting                               | Key           | Default | Level | What it does                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                        |\n| ------------------------------------- | ------------- | ------- | ----- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| **Drugs, alcohol, betting and dares** | `topics.risk` | default | basic | How MaiPai answers a child's questions about medicine, drugs, alcohol, vaping, betting and dangerous dares. The standard answer explains simply that these are unsafe or for adults. Only a parent or admin can change a child's. It applies only while the person is on child controls and never reaches the care, safety and fairness rules, which stay the same for every child. |","table":"table-23"},"527":{"id":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference-186","page_id":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference#person-profile--topics-sensitive-subjects","content":"| Setting                              | Key               | Default | Level | What it does                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                             |\n| ------------------------------------ | ----------------- | ------- | ----- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| **Violence, weapons and scary news** | `topics.violence` | default | basic | How MaiPai answers a child's questions about violence, weapons, war, scary news and scary stories. The standard answer says what happened without gore and that helpers keep people safe. Only a parent or admin can change a child's. It applies only while the person is on child controls and never reaches the care, safety and fairness rules, which stay the same for every child. |","table":"table-23"},"528":{"id":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference-187","page_id":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference#person-profile--topics-sensitive-subjects","content":"| Setting                                  | Key                     | Default | Level | What it does                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                        |\n| ---------------------------------------- | ----------------------- | ------- | ----- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| **Santa Claus and other family stories** | `topics.family_stories` | keep    | basic | Whether MaiPai keeps stories like Santa Claus, the Tooth Fairy and the Easter Bunny for a child: it never says whether they are real, plays along, and points the child to the family. Turn it off if you would rather MaiPai answered plainly. Only a parent or admin can change a child's. It applies only while the person is on child controls. |","table":"table-23"},"529":{"id":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference-188","page_id":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference#person-profile--topics-sensitive-subjects","content":"| Setting                     | Key                         | Default                                        | Level | What it does                                                                                                                                                                   |\n| --------------------------- | --------------------------- | ---------------------------------------------- | ----- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| **Names of family stories** | `topics.family_story_names` | Santa Claus, the Tooth Fairy, the Easter Bunny | basic | The stories MaiPai keeps for this child, separated by commas. Add your family's own, such as Elf on the Shelf or the Three Kings. Only a parent or admin can change a child's. |","table":"table-23"},"530":{"id":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference-189","page_id":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference#personal-settings--voice","content":"| Setting            | Key            | Default | Level | What it does                                                  |\n| ------------------ | -------------- | ------- | ----- | ------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| **Speaking voice** | `tts.voice_id` | alba    | basic | The voice MaiPai uses when it reads its replies aloud to you. |","table":"table-24"},"531":{"id":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference-190","page_id":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference#personal-settings--appearance--appearance","content":"| Setting                       | Key                       | Default | Level | What it does                                                                                  |\n| ----------------------------- | ------------------------- | ------- | ----- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| **Start tours automatically** | `tours.autostart.enabled` | on      | basic | A guide opens on a page's first visit when enabled. Help can open Show me around at any time. |","table":"table-25"},"532":{"id":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference-191","page_id":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference#personal-settings--appearance--appearance","content":"| Setting        | Key             | Default | Level | What it does                                     |\n| -------------- | --------------- | ------- | ----- | ------------------------------------------------ |\n| **Appearance** | `ui.appearance` | system  | basic | Light, dark, or match this device's own setting. |","table":"table-25"},"533":{"id":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference-192","page_id":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference#personal-settings--appearance--appearance","content":"| Setting  | Key       | Default | Level | What it does                                                                                                                                     |\n| -------- | --------- | ------- | ----- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| **Look** | `ui.look` | neutral | basic | Neutral is the standard black-and-white theme, the same as shadcn's own dashboard; the rest are shadcn's other color sets; Navy is MaiPai's own. |","table":"table-25"},"534":{"id":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference-193","page_id":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference#personal-settings--appearance--appearance","content":"| Setting                    | Key              | Default | Level  | What it does                                                                                                                 |\n| -------------------------- | ---------------- | ------- | ------ | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| **Pinned apps (advanced)** | `ui.pinned_apps` | []      | expert | A JSON list of nav entry ids, in the order they should appear. Normally set by pinning an app, not by editing this directly. |","table":"table-25"},"535":{"id":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference-194","page_id":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference#personal-settings--appearance--appearance","content":"| Setting                          | Key                         | Default | Level  | What it does                                                                |\n| -------------------------------- | --------------------------- | ------- | ------ | --------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| **Setup checklist items hidden** | `setup.checklist_dismissed` | []      | expert | A JSON list of setup checklist item ids this person chose not to see again. |","table":"table-25"},"536":{"id":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference-195","page_id":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference#personal-settings--appearance--ease-of-use","content":"| Setting           | Key           | Default  | Level | What it does                                                                                                                                                                                                           |\n| ----------------- | ------------- | -------- | ----- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| **Comfort style** | `ease.preset` | standard | basic | A bundle of comfort settings: text size, spacing, button size, contrast, calm and helpers. Pick one, then change any single setting below. It is about comfort, not age, and it never changes what is safe or allowed. |","table":"table-26"},"537":{"id":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference-196","page_id":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference#personal-settings--appearance--ease-of-use","content":"| Setting       | Key              | Default | Level | What it does                                                               |\n| ------------- | ---------------- | ------- | ----- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| **Text size** | `ease.text_size` | preset  | basic | Percent of the normal text size. \"Preset\" follows your ease of use choice. |","table":"table-26"},"538":{"id":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference-197","page_id":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference#personal-settings--appearance--ease-of-use","content":"| Setting     | Key            | Default | Level | What it does                                                                     |\n| ----------- | -------------- | ------- | ----- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| **Spacing** | `ease.spacing` | preset  | basic | How much room there is between things. \"Preset\" follows your ease of use choice. |","table":"table-26"},"539":{"id":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference-198","page_id":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference#personal-settings--appearance--ease-of-use","content":"| Setting         | Key            | Default | Level | What it does                                                                                              |\n| --------------- | -------------- | ------- | ----- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| **Button size** | `ease.targets` | preset  | basic | The smallest size of a button or tap area. Large is about 2 cm. \"Preset\" follows your ease of use choice. |","table":"table-26"},"540":{"id":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference-199","page_id":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference#personal-settings--appearance--ease-of-use","content":"| Setting      | Key             | Default | Level | What it does                                                                   |\n| ------------ | --------------- | ------- | ----- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| **Contrast** | `ease.contrast` | preset  | basic | More makes text stand out at 7 to 1. \"Preset\" follows your ease of use choice. |","table":"table-26"},"541":{"id":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference-200","page_id":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference#personal-settings--appearance--ease-of-use","content":"| Setting              | Key           | Default | Level | What it does                                                                     |\n| -------------------- | ------------- | ------- | ----- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| **Motion and color** | `ease.motion` | preset  | basic | Calm mutes colors and stops animation. \"Preset\" follows your ease of use choice. |","table":"table-26"},"542":{"id":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference-201","page_id":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference#personal-settings--appearance--ease-of-use","content":"| Setting         | Key                | Default | Level | What it does                                                                                                                      |\n| --------------- | ------------------ | ------- | ----- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| **Simple mode** | `ease.simple_mode` | preset  | basic | Shows only the main apps and settings and hides the rest. It hides, it does not forbid. \"Preset\" follows your ease of use choice. |","table":"table-26"},"543":{"id":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference-202","page_id":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference#personal-settings--appearance--ease-of-use","content":"| Setting           | Key                  | Default  | Level | What it does                                                                                                                                                    |\n| ----------------- | -------------------- | -------- | ----- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| **Reading level** | `ease.reading_level` | standard | basic | How plainly MaiPai words its answers and app text: standard, plain or very simple. It changes words and sentence shape only, never what MaiPai will talk about. |","table":"table-26"},"544":{"id":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference-203","page_id":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference#personal-settings--appearance--ease-of-use","content":"| Setting              | Key               | Default | Level | What it does                                                                                                                    |\n| -------------------- | ----------------- | ------- | ----- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| **Short explainers** | `ease.explainers` | preset  | basic | Shows a short note at the top of a screen about what it is for, until you dismiss it. \"Preset\" follows your ease of use choice. |","table":"table-26"},"545":{"id":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference-204","page_id":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference#personal-settings--appearance--ease-of-use","content":"| Setting       | Key              | Default | Level | What it does                                                                                |\n| ------------- | ---------------- | ------- | ----- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| **Word help** | `ease.word_help` | preset  | basic | Press a word to see what it means in plain words. \"Preset\" follows your ease of use choice. |","table":"table-26"},"546":{"id":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference-205","page_id":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference#personal-settings--appearance--ease-of-use","content":"| Setting        | Key               | Default | Level | What it does                                                                                                  |\n| -------------- | ----------------- | ------- | ----- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| **Read aloud** | `ease.read_aloud` | preset  | basic | Adds a button to read replies and news aloud in MaiPai's own voice. \"Preset\" follows your ease of use choice. |","table":"table-26"},"547":{"id":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference-206","page_id":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference#robot-settings-1","content":"| Setting                              | Key                      | Default | Level | What it does                                                                       |\n| ------------------------------------ | ------------------------ | ------- | ----- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| **Robot may listen for a follow-up** | `person.robot.follow_up` | on      | basic | Adults and teens are on by default. Children are off unless a parent enables this. |","table":"table-27"},"548":{"id":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference-207","page_id":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference#robot-settings-1","content":"| Setting                     | Key                          | Default | Level | What it does                                                                                             |\n| --------------------------- | ---------------------------- | ------- | ----- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| **Robot may greet by name** | `person.robot.greet_by_name` | on      | basic | Adults are on by default; children are off until a parent enables this. Teens control their own setting. |","table":"table-27"},"549":{"id":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference-208","page_id":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference#robot-settings-1","content":"| Setting                           | Key                        | Default | Level | What it does                                                                                             |\n| --------------------------------- | -------------------------- | ------- | ----- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| **Robot may address this person** | `person.robot.may_address` | on      | basic | Adults are on by default. Children are off until a parent enables this; teens control their own setting. |","table":"table-27"},"550":{"id":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference-209","page_id":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference#robot-settings-1","content":"| Setting                       | Key                          | Default | Level | What it does                                                                                             |\n| ----------------------------- | ---------------------------- | ------- | ----- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| **Allow playful robot clips** | `person.robot.playful_clips` | on      | basic | Adults are on by default; children are off until a parent enables this. Teens control their own setting. |","table":"table-27"},"551":{"id":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference-210","page_id":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference#robot-settings-1","content":"| Setting                       | Key                   | Default | Level | What it does                                                                                                                                       |\n| ----------------------------- | --------------------- | ------- | ----- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| **Robot conversation topics** | `person.robot.topics` | nudges  | basic | Controls optional nudges and chit-chat. Adults get nudges on and chit-chat off by default; children get both off. Teens control their own setting. |","table":"table-27"},"552":{"id":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference-211","page_id":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference#robot-settings-1","content":"| Setting                         | Key                      | Default | Level | What it does                                                                            |\n| ------------------------------- | ------------------------ | ------- | ----- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| **Allow robot gesture sensing** | `person.vision.gestures` | on      | basic | On by default; a parent can change a child setting and teens control their own setting. |","table":"table-27"},"553":{"id":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference-212","page_id":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference#robot-settings-1","content":"| Setting                      | Key                   | Default  | Level | What it does                                                                                                                                                              |\n| ---------------------------- | --------------------- | -------- | ----- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| **Robot vision watch level** | `person.vision.watch` | presence | basic | Identity is used only for enrolled people. Children stay at presence until a parent chooses; teens control their own setting. The stricter person and robot levels apply. |","table":"table-27"},"554":{"id":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference-213","page_id":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference#personal-settings--commands-weather","content":"| Setting            | Key              | Default | Level | What it does                   |\n| ------------------ | ---------------- | ------- | ----- | ------------------------------ |\n| **Weather places** | `weather.places` | []      | basic | Places saved for this surface. |","table":"table-28"},"555":{"id":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference-214","page_id":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference#personal-settings--commands-weather","content":"| Setting                   | Key                     | Default | Level | What it does                               |\n| ------------------------- | ----------------------- | ------- | ----- | ------------------------------------------ |\n| **Weather default place** | `weather.default_place` | current | basic | The place used by default on this surface. |","table":"table-28"},"556":{"id":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference-215","page_id":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference#robot-hello-this-device","content":"| Setting                        | Key                       | Default | Level    | What it does                                                                                                                |\n| ------------------------------ | ------------------------- | ------- | -------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| **Full open-mic interruption** | `robot.barge_in.open_mic` | off     | advanced | Robot-only device setting delivered by Home as settings_changed. Off until arrival-day echo-cancellation measurements pass. |","table":"table-29"},"557":{"id":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference-216","page_id":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference#robot-hello-this-device","content":"| Setting                      | Key                        | Default  | Level | What it does                                                                                                                 |\n| ---------------------------- | -------------------------- | -------- | ----- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| **Robot camera watch level** | `robot.camera.watch_level` | identify | basic | Robot-only device setting delivered by Home as settings_changed. The stricter of this and each person’s watch level applies. |","table":"table-29"},"558":{"id":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference-217","page_id":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference#robot-hello-this-device","content":"| Setting                    | Key                       | Default | Level | What it does                                                                                                                           |\n| -------------------------- | ------------------------- | ------- | ----- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| **Robot follow-up window** | `robot.follow_up.seconds` | 8       | basic | Robot-only device setting delivered by Home as settings_changed. 0 disables the window; child access still requires the person switch. |","table":"table-29"},"559":{"id":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference-218","page_id":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference#robot-hello-this-device","content":"| Setting                   | Key                      | Default | Level | What it does                                                                                                             |\n| ------------------------- | ------------------------ | ------- | ----- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| **Robot gesture sensing** | `robot.gestures.enabled` | off     | basic | Robot-only device setting delivered by Home as settings_changed. Packages may explicitly arm gestures while this is off. |","table":"table-29"},"560":{"id":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference-219","page_id":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference#robot-hello-this-device","content":"| Setting                 | Key                | Default | Level | What it does                                                     |\n| ----------------------- | ------------------ | ------- | ----- | ---------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| **Robot idle movement** | `robot.idle.level` | calm    | basic | Robot-only device setting delivered by Home as settings_changed. |","table":"table-29"},"561":{"id":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference-220","page_id":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference#robot-hello-this-device","content":"| Setting                       | Key                             | Default | Level | What it does                                                                                                    |\n| ----------------------------- | ------------------------------- | ------- | ----- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| **Allow offers in this room** | `robot.initiative.allowed_here` | off     | basic | Robot-only device setting delivered by Home as settings_changed. Off until an admin allows offers in this room. |","table":"table-29"},"562":{"id":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference-221","page_id":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/settings-reference#robot-hello-this-device","content":"| Setting                       | Key                | Default | Level | What it does                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                               |\n| ----------------------------- | ------------------ | ------- | ----- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| **Sleep when dark and quiet** | `robot.sleep.auto` | on      | basic | On by default. This robot goes to sleep after 10 minutes of darkness and no speech, and during household quiet hours. A face, speech or a knock wakes it, and the wake word still works. Turn off to keep it awake. Only an admin changes this, for each robot on its own. |","table":"table-29"},"563":{"id":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/use-another-computer-for-the-ai","page_id":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/use-another-computer-for-the-ai","type":"page","content":"Use another computer for the AI","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Admin guide","🛠️ Install and set up"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/use-another-computer-for-the-ai"},"564":{"id":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/use-another-computer-for-the-ai-0","page_id":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/use-another-computer-for-the-ai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/use-another-computer-for-the-ai","content":"Run the AI engines on a second Ubuntu computer and pair it with Home."},"565":{"id":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/use-another-computer-for-the-ai-1","page_id":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/use-another-computer-for-the-ai","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/use-another-computer-for-the-ai#-before-you-start","content":"✅ Before you start"},"566":{"id":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/use-another-computer-for-the-ai-2","page_id":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/use-another-computer-for-the-ai","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/use-another-computer-for-the-ai#-set-up-the-engine-computer","content":"🔧 Set up the engine computer"},"567":{"id":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/use-another-computer-for-the-ai-3","page_id":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/use-another-computer-for-the-ai","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/use-another-computer-for-the-ai#-pair-it-with-home","content":"🔗 Pair it with Home"},"568":{"id":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/use-another-computer-for-the-ai-4","page_id":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/use-another-computer-for-the-ai","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/use-another-computer-for-the-ai#-check-it-later","content":"🩺 Check it later"},"569":{"id":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/use-another-computer-for-the-ai-5","page_id":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/use-another-computer-for-the-ai","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/use-another-computer-for-the-ai#️-unpair","content":"✂️ Unpair"},"570":{"id":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/use-another-computer-for-the-ai-6","page_id":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/use-another-computer-for-the-ai","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/use-another-computer-for-the-ai#-away-from-home","content":"🌍 Away from home"},"571":{"id":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/use-another-computer-for-the-ai-7","page_id":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/use-another-computer-for-the-ai","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/use-another-computer-for-the-ai#-if-chat-stops-answering","content":"🔧 If chat stops answering"},"572":{"id":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/use-another-computer-for-the-ai-8","page_id":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/use-another-computer-for-the-ai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/use-another-computer-for-the-ai","content":"Home can use the AI engines (the Stack) on the same computer, or on a second computer in your home. A second computer is useful when it has a stronger graphics card or more memory than the one running Home."},"573":{"id":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/use-another-computer-for-the-ai-9","page_id":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/use-another-computer-for-the-ai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/use-another-computer-for-the-ai#-before-you-start","content":"The second computer runs Ubuntu Linux. Other systems are not supported for this."},"574":{"id":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/use-another-computer-for-the-ai-10","page_id":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/use-another-computer-for-the-ai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/use-another-computer-for-the-ai#-before-you-start","content":"Both computers are on the same home network."},"575":{"id":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/use-another-computer-for-the-ai-11","page_id":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/use-another-computer-for-the-ai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/use-another-computer-for-the-ai#-before-you-start","content":"You can use `sudo` on the engine computer."},"576":{"id":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/use-another-computer-for-the-ai-12","page_id":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/use-another-computer-for-the-ai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/use-another-computer-for-the-ai#-set-up-the-engine-computer","content":"On the engine computer, run the installer with the engine option."},"577":{"id":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/use-another-computer-for-the-ai-13","page_id":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/use-another-computer-for-the-ai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/use-another-computer-for-the-ai#-set-up-the-engine-computer","content":"The installer creates a `maipai-stack` service user, installs the Stack under `/opt/maipai-stack`, keeps its data in `/data/stack`, and enables SSH, asking first if `openssh-server` is missing. It then installs the `maipai-engine` tool."},"578":{"id":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/use-another-computer-for-the-ai-14","page_id":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/use-another-computer-for-the-ai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/use-another-computer-for-the-ai#-set-up-the-engine-computer","content":"Wait for \"Ready to pair.\""},"579":{"id":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/use-another-computer-for-the-ai-15","page_id":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/use-another-computer-for-the-ai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/use-another-computer-for-the-ai#-pair-it-with-home","content":"In Home, open **Settings**, **Home settings**, **Engines and AI**."},"580":{"id":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/use-another-computer-for-the-ai-16","page_id":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/use-another-computer-for-the-ai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/use-another-computer-for-the-ai#-pair-it-with-home","content":"Press **Pair engine computer**."},"581":{"id":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/use-another-computer-for-the-ai-17","page_id":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/use-another-computer-for-the-ai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/use-another-computer-for-the-ai#-pair-it-with-home","content":"Pick **Another computer**, then **Next**."},"582":{"id":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/use-another-computer-for-the-ai-18","page_id":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/use-another-computer-for-the-ai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/use-another-computer-for-the-ai#-pair-it-with-home","content":"Type the engine computer's name or home network address, for example `192.0.2.20`, and its SSH port (usually 22)."},"583":{"id":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/use-another-computer-for-the-ai-19","page_id":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/use-another-computer-for-the-ai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/use-another-computer-for-the-ai#-pair-it-with-home","content":"Press **Get a one-time code**. Home shows a command like `sudo maipai-engine pair https://home.example ABCD-EFGH-JKLM`. Copy it."},"584":{"id":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/use-another-computer-for-the-ai-20","page_id":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/use-another-computer-for-the-ai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/use-another-computer-for-the-ai#-pair-it-with-home","content":"Run that command on the engine computer. The code works once and Home shows when it expires. The command prints a **check code**."},"585":{"id":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/use-another-computer-for-the-ai-21","page_id":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/use-another-computer-for-the-ai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/use-another-computer-for-the-ai#-pair-it-with-home","content":"Back in Home, press **Check the engine computer**, type the check code, then press **Pin this computer**."},"586":{"id":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/use-another-computer-for-the-ai-22","page_id":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/use-another-computer-for-the-ai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/use-another-computer-for-the-ai#-pair-it-with-home","content":"Home reads the computer's security key and compares the check code, so you know you are talking to your machine and not another one."},"587":{"id":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/use-another-computer-for-the-ai-23","page_id":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/use-another-computer-for-the-ai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/use-another-computer-for-the-ai#-pair-it-with-home","content":"Home runs a hop-by-hop connection test and shows **PASS** or **FAIL** for each hop with the fix."},"588":{"id":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/use-another-computer-for-the-ai-24","page_id":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/use-another-computer-for-the-ai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/use-another-computer-for-the-ai#-check-it-later","content":"**Engines** shows **Engine health** and a **Check the connection** button."},"589":{"id":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/use-another-computer-for-the-ai-25","page_id":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/use-another-computer-for-the-ai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/use-another-computer-for-the-ai#-check-it-later","content":"On the engine computer, `sudo maipai-engine status` and `sudo maipai-engine doctor` report what is running."},"590":{"id":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/use-another-computer-for-the-ai-26","page_id":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/use-another-computer-for-the-ai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/use-another-computer-for-the-ai#-check-it-later","content":"**Needs restart** or **Update available** on a row means exactly that."},"591":{"id":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/use-another-computer-for-the-ai-27","page_id":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/use-another-computer-for-the-ai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/use-another-computer-for-the-ai#️-unpair","content":"On the engine computer, run `sudo maipai-engine unpair`."},"592":{"id":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/use-another-computer-for-the-ai-28","page_id":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/use-another-computer-for-the-ai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/use-another-computer-for-the-ai#️-unpair","content":"In Home, press **Revoke link key**."},"593":{"id":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/use-another-computer-for-the-ai-29","page_id":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/use-another-computer-for-the-ai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/use-another-computer-for-the-ai#-away-from-home","content":"Reaching the engine computer through Tailscale is off by default. Turn on the `engines.stack.remote.allow_tailnet` setting only after you have joined both computers to your Tailscale network yourself. See Remote access."},"594":{"id":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/use-another-computer-for-the-ai-30","page_id":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/use-another-computer-for-the-ai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/admin/install-and-set-up/use-another-computer-for-the-ai#-if-chat-stops-answering","content":"**Engines** says \"No Stack configured\" when no engine is set. Open **Where the engine runs**, pick one, and run **Check the connection**. The page for the Home computer is at Troubleshooting."},"595":{"id":"/docs/admin/look-after-it/backups-and-restore","page_id":"/docs/admin/look-after-it/backups-and-restore","type":"page","content":"Backups and restore","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Admin guide","🩺 Look after it"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/admin/look-after-it/backups-and-restore"},"596":{"id":"/docs/admin/look-after-it/backups-and-restore-0","page_id":"/docs/admin/look-after-it/backups-and-restore","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/admin/look-after-it/backups-and-restore","content":"How Home backs itself up, how to take one now, and how to restore."},"597":{"id":"/docs/admin/look-after-it/backups-and-restore-1","page_id":"/docs/admin/look-after-it/backups-and-restore","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/admin/look-after-it/backups-and-restore#-what-happens-on-its-own","content":"⏰ What happens on its own"},"598":{"id":"/docs/admin/look-after-it/backups-and-restore-2","page_id":"/docs/admin/look-after-it/backups-and-restore","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/admin/look-after-it/backups-and-restore#-save-your-backup-key","content":"🔑 Save your backup key"},"599":{"id":"/docs/admin/look-after-it/backups-and-restore-3","page_id":"/docs/admin/look-after-it/backups-and-restore","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/admin/look-after-it/backups-and-restore#-back-up-now","content":"💾 Back up now"},"600":{"id":"/docs/admin/look-after-it/backups-and-restore-4","page_id":"/docs/admin/look-after-it/backups-and-restore","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/admin/look-after-it/backups-and-restore#️-restore","content":"♻️ Restore"},"601":{"id":"/docs/admin/look-after-it/backups-and-restore-5","page_id":"/docs/admin/look-after-it/backups-and-restore","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/admin/look-after-it/backups-and-restore#️-a-second-copy","content":"🗄️ A second copy"},"602":{"id":"/docs/admin/look-after-it/backups-and-restore-6","page_id":"/docs/admin/look-after-it/backups-and-restore","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/admin/look-after-it/backups-and-restore#-practice","content":"🧪 Practice"},"603":{"id":"/docs/admin/look-after-it/backups-and-restore-7","page_id":"/docs/admin/look-after-it/backups-and-restore","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/admin/look-after-it/backups-and-restore","content":"A backup is one encrypted copy of Home's household database: people, memories, conversations and settings. Models, engines, the reference library and uploaded files are not in it. Those are downloaded or copied again after a restore."},"604":{"id":"/docs/admin/look-after-it/backups-and-restore-8","page_id":"/docs/admin/look-after-it/backups-and-restore","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/admin/look-after-it/backups-and-restore#-what-happens-on-its-own","content":"Home takes a backup **every day**."},"605":{"id":"/docs/admin/look-after-it/backups-and-restore-9","page_id":"/docs/admin/look-after-it/backups-and-restore","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/admin/look-after-it/backups-and-restore#-what-happens-on-its-own","content":"It keeps **7 daily**, **4 weekly** and **3 monthly** copies, and deletes older ones."},"606":{"id":"/docs/admin/look-after-it/backups-and-restore-10","page_id":"/docs/admin/look-after-it/backups-and-restore","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/admin/look-after-it/backups-and-restore#-what-happens-on-its-own","content":"**Backup storage limit (GB)** under Storage and backups is 0 by default, which means no limit. Set a number and Home deletes the oldest first to stay under it."},"607":{"id":"/docs/admin/look-after-it/backups-and-restore-11","page_id":"/docs/admin/look-after-it/backups-and-restore","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/admin/look-after-it/backups-and-restore#-what-happens-on-its-own","content":"Backups go in the `backups` folder beside the data folder. Files are named `backup-<time>-<suffix>.db.enc`."},"608":{"id":"/docs/admin/look-after-it/backups-and-restore-12","page_id":"/docs/admin/look-after-it/backups-and-restore","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/admin/look-after-it/backups-and-restore#-what-happens-on-its-own","content":"A backup on the same disk as Home does not survive that disk failing. Copy the `backups` folder to another disk or computer regularly."},"609":{"id":"/docs/admin/look-after-it/backups-and-restore-13","page_id":"/docs/admin/look-after-it/backups-and-restore","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/admin/look-after-it/backups-and-restore#-save-your-backup-key","content":"Backups are encrypted. The **backup key** is what lets a new computer read them. The setup wizard offers **Save your backup key** at the end, with **Download** and **Print**. The file is `maipai-home-emergency-backup-key.txt`. Saving the key later from **Settings**, **Backups** gives the same file name."},"610":{"id":"/docs/admin/look-after-it/backups-and-restore-14","page_id":"/docs/admin/look-after-it/backups-and-restore","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/admin/look-after-it/backups-and-restore#-save-your-backup-key","content":"Keep it somewhere other than the Home computer, such as a password manager or a printed page in a drawer. Without it, a restore on a new computer cannot read the backups."},"611":{"id":"/docs/admin/look-after-it/backups-and-restore-15","page_id":"/docs/admin/look-after-it/backups-and-restore","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/admin/look-after-it/backups-and-restore#-save-your-backup-key","content":"If Home fails to make the key, it says \"Home couldn't make your backup key. Press Download again.\" If it fails again, open Repairs."},"612":{"id":"/docs/admin/look-after-it/backups-and-restore-16","page_id":"/docs/admin/look-after-it/backups-and-restore","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/admin/look-after-it/backups-and-restore#-back-up-now","content":"Open **Settings**, then **Home settings**, then **Storage and backups**, then **Backups**."},"613":{"id":"/docs/admin/look-after-it/backups-and-restore-17","page_id":"/docs/admin/look-after-it/backups-and-restore","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/admin/look-after-it/backups-and-restore#-back-up-now","content":"Press **Back up now**."},"614":{"id":"/docs/admin/look-after-it/backups-and-restore-18","page_id":"/docs/admin/look-after-it/backups-and-restore","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/admin/look-after-it/backups-and-restore#-back-up-now","content":"The new copy appears in the table with its date and size."},"615":{"id":"/docs/admin/look-after-it/backups-and-restore-19","page_id":"/docs/admin/look-after-it/backups-and-restore","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/admin/look-after-it/backups-and-restore#-back-up-now","content":"Owners and admins can do this. A new household shows \"No backups yet.\" until the first run."},"616":{"id":"/docs/admin/look-after-it/backups-and-restore-20","page_id":"/docs/admin/look-after-it/backups-and-restore","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/admin/look-after-it/backups-and-restore#️-restore","content":"Only the owner can restore."},"617":{"id":"/docs/admin/look-after-it/backups-and-restore-21","page_id":"/docs/admin/look-after-it/backups-and-restore","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/admin/look-after-it/backups-and-restore#️-restore","content":"Open **Backups**."},"618":{"id":"/docs/admin/look-after-it/backups-and-restore-22","page_id":"/docs/admin/look-after-it/backups-and-restore","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/admin/look-after-it/backups-and-restore#️-restore","content":"Press **Restore** on the row you want and confirm."},"619":{"id":"/docs/admin/look-after-it/backups-and-restore-23","page_id":"/docs/admin/look-after-it/backups-and-restore","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/admin/look-after-it/backups-and-restore#️-restore","content":"A **Ready to restore** banner appears. Restart Home."},"620":{"id":"/docs/admin/look-after-it/backups-and-restore-24","page_id":"/docs/admin/look-after-it/backups-and-restore","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/admin/look-after-it/backups-and-restore#️-restore","content":"At the next start Home swaps in the restored database."},"621":{"id":"/docs/admin/look-after-it/backups-and-restore-25","page_id":"/docs/admin/look-after-it/backups-and-restore","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/admin/look-after-it/backups-and-restore#️-restore","content":"Before it swaps, Home takes a fresh backup and checks the archive. If the file cannot be read, Home says \"that backup could not be read. Try another one.\" Press **Cancel restore** on the banner to change your mind before restarting."},"622":{"id":"/docs/admin/look-after-it/backups-and-restore-26","page_id":"/docs/admin/look-after-it/backups-and-restore","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/admin/look-after-it/backups-and-restore#️-restore","content":"The database you replaced is kept as `hub.db.pre-restore`. Keep it until you are sure the restore is right."},"623":{"id":"/docs/admin/look-after-it/backups-and-restore-27","page_id":"/docs/admin/look-after-it/backups-and-restore","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/admin/look-after-it/backups-and-restore#️-a-second-copy","content":"Home can also copy backups to a mounted folder, such as a NAS share. Planned, not in the app yet: a screen for it. Today the folder is set through the Home API by an owner or admin. If that copy starts failing, Home raises a **Repairs** item and can message you on Telegram. See Notifications and Telegram."},"624":{"id":"/docs/admin/look-after-it/backups-and-restore-28","page_id":"/docs/admin/look-after-it/backups-and-restore","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/admin/look-after-it/backups-and-restore#-practice","content":"A restore you have never tried is a guess. Once, on a spare computer, install Home, restore a backup with your saved key and sign in."},"625":{"id":"/docs/admin/look-after-it/devices-and-sessions","page_id":"/docs/admin/look-after-it/devices-and-sessions","type":"page","content":"Devices and signed-in sessions","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Admin guide","🩺 Look after it"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/admin/look-after-it/devices-and-sessions"},"626":{"id":"/docs/admin/look-after-it/devices-and-sessions-0","page_id":"/docs/admin/look-after-it/devices-and-sessions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/admin/look-after-it/devices-and-sessions","content":"See what is paired to your profile and sign out a browser you no longer use."},"627":{"id":"/docs/admin/look-after-it/devices-and-sessions-1","page_id":"/docs/admin/look-after-it/devices-and-sessions","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/admin/look-after-it/devices-and-sessions#️-steps","content":"✍️ Steps"},"628":{"id":"/docs/admin/look-after-it/devices-and-sessions-2","page_id":"/docs/admin/look-after-it/devices-and-sessions","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/admin/look-after-it/devices-and-sessions#-still-need-help","content":"🙋 Still need help?"},"629":{"id":"/docs/admin/look-after-it/devices-and-sessions-3","page_id":"/docs/admin/look-after-it/devices-and-sessions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/admin/look-after-it/devices-and-sessions","content":"This page shows your own devices and sessions. It is not a household list."},"630":{"id":"/docs/admin/look-after-it/devices-and-sessions-4","page_id":"/docs/admin/look-after-it/devices-and-sessions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/admin/look-after-it/devices-and-sessions#️-steps","content":"Open **Settings**, **Data and privacy**, then **Signed-in devices**."},"631":{"id":"/docs/admin/look-after-it/devices-and-sessions-5","page_id":"/docs/admin/look-after-it/devices-and-sessions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/admin/look-after-it/devices-and-sessions#️-steps","content":"Under **Devices** you see paired robots, pods, TVs, phones, desktops and browsers, with the room and when each was last seen. A device that never connected says \"never connected\"."},"632":{"id":"/docs/admin/look-after-it/devices-and-sessions-6","page_id":"/docs/admin/look-after-it/devices-and-sessions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/admin/look-after-it/devices-and-sessions#️-steps","content":"Tap **Remove** beside one, then **Yes, remove it**. It must be paired again to reconnect. **Keep it** cancels."},"633":{"id":"/docs/admin/look-after-it/devices-and-sessions-7","page_id":"/docs/admin/look-after-it/devices-and-sessions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/admin/look-after-it/devices-and-sessions#️-steps","content":"Under **Signed-in sessions**, tap **Sign out** beside another browser, then **Yes, sign it out**."},"634":{"id":"/docs/admin/look-after-it/devices-and-sessions-8","page_id":"/docs/admin/look-after-it/devices-and-sessions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/admin/look-after-it/devices-and-sessions#️-steps","content":"Your current session shows **This device** and has no sign-out button. Use **Log out** in the profile menu for that."},"635":{"id":"/docs/admin/look-after-it/devices-and-sessions-9","page_id":"/docs/admin/look-after-it/devices-and-sessions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/admin/look-after-it/devices-and-sessions#️-steps","content":"If nothing is paired, you see \"No devices paired to your profile yet.\""},"636":{"id":"/docs/admin/look-after-it/devices-and-sessions-10","page_id":"/docs/admin/look-after-it/devices-and-sessions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/admin/look-after-it/devices-and-sessions#-still-need-help","content":"If a list will not load, reload the page. If it keeps failing, see Troubleshooting and support report."},"637":{"id":"/docs/admin/look-after-it/performance","page_id":"/docs/admin/look-after-it/performance","type":"page","content":"Performance","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Admin guide","🩺 Look after it"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/admin/look-after-it/performance"},"638":{"id":"/docs/admin/look-after-it/performance-0","page_id":"/docs/admin/look-after-it/performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/admin/look-after-it/performance","content":"See how replies, queues and engines are doing over time."},"639":{"id":"/docs/admin/look-after-it/performance-1","page_id":"/docs/admin/look-after-it/performance","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/admin/look-after-it/performance#️-steps","content":"✍️ Steps"},"640":{"id":"/docs/admin/look-after-it/performance-2","page_id":"/docs/admin/look-after-it/performance","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/admin/look-after-it/performance#-still-need-help","content":"🙋 Still need help?"},"641":{"id":"/docs/admin/look-after-it/performance-3","page_id":"/docs/admin/look-after-it/performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/admin/look-after-it/performance","content":"This page is for owners and admins. Other roles are refused."},"642":{"id":"/docs/admin/look-after-it/performance-4","page_id":"/docs/admin/look-after-it/performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/admin/look-after-it/performance#️-steps","content":"Open **Settings**, **Home settings**, **Maintenance**, then **Performance**."},"643":{"id":"/docs/admin/look-after-it/performance-5","page_id":"/docs/admin/look-after-it/performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/admin/look-after-it/performance#️-steps","content":"Read the cards:"},"644":{"id":"/docs/admin/look-after-it/performance-6","page_id":"/docs/admin/look-after-it/performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/admin/look-after-it/performance#️-steps","content":"| Card                   | What it shows                   |\n| ---------------------- | ------------------------------- |\n| **Reply time per day** | How long replies took each day. |","table":"table-0"},"645":{"id":"/docs/admin/look-after-it/performance-7","page_id":"/docs/admin/look-after-it/performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/admin/look-after-it/performance#️-steps","content":"| Card       | What it shows                                                       |\n| ---------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| **Queues** | Waiting work: **Memory judge**, **Embedding retry**, **Ingestion**. |","table":"table-0"},"646":{"id":"/docs/admin/look-after-it/performance-8","page_id":"/docs/admin/look-after-it/performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/admin/look-after-it/performance#️-steps","content":"| Card                 | What it shows          |\n| -------------------- | ---------------------- |\n| **Turns per engine** | Which engine answered. |","table":"table-0"},"647":{"id":"/docs/admin/look-after-it/performance-9","page_id":"/docs/admin/look-after-it/performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/admin/look-after-it/performance#️-steps","content":"| Card            | What it shows                  |\n| --------------- | ------------------------------ |\n| **Route taken** | Which path each turn followed. |","table":"table-0"},"648":{"id":"/docs/admin/look-after-it/performance-10","page_id":"/docs/admin/look-after-it/performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/admin/look-after-it/performance#️-steps","content":"| Card       | What it shows                      |\n| ---------- | ---------------------------------- |\n| **Layers** | Time spent in each step of a turn. |","table":"table-0"},"649":{"id":"/docs/admin/look-after-it/performance-11","page_id":"/docs/admin/look-after-it/performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/admin/look-after-it/performance#️-steps","content":"| Card              | What it shows                              |\n| ----------------- | ------------------------------------------ |\n| **Label harvest** | How many turns were counted in the window. |","table":"table-0"},"650":{"id":"/docs/admin/look-after-it/performance-12","page_id":"/docs/admin/look-after-it/performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/admin/look-after-it/performance#️-steps","content":"| Card        | What it shows  |\n| ----------- | -------------- |\n| **Engines** | Engine health. |","table":"table-0"},"651":{"id":"/docs/admin/look-after-it/performance-13","page_id":"/docs/admin/look-after-it/performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/admin/look-after-it/performance#️-steps","content":"| Card                   | What it shows              |\n| ---------------------- | -------------------------- |\n| **Storage & hardware** | Disk and computer details. |","table":"table-0"},"652":{"id":"/docs/admin/look-after-it/performance-14","page_id":"/docs/admin/look-after-it/performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/admin/look-after-it/performance#️-steps","content":"The numbers come from what Home already records. Nothing new is collected, and nothing leaves the house."},"653":{"id":"/docs/admin/look-after-it/performance-15","page_id":"/docs/admin/look-after-it/performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/admin/look-after-it/performance#️-steps","content":"**Layers** says \"No traced turns yet\" until a turn has left a timing trace."},"654":{"id":"/docs/admin/look-after-it/performance-16","page_id":"/docs/admin/look-after-it/performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/admin/look-after-it/performance#️-steps","content":"If the page fails, it says \"Could not load performance.\" Reload it. See Troubleshooting."},"655":{"id":"/docs/admin/look-after-it/performance-17","page_id":"/docs/admin/look-after-it/performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/admin/look-after-it/performance#-still-need-help","content":"If a queue keeps growing, open **Status** in **Maintenance** and check the engines."},"656":{"id":"/docs/admin/look-after-it/privacy-audit","page_id":"/docs/admin/look-after-it/privacy-audit","type":"page","content":"Privacy audit","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Admin guide","🩺 Look after it"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/admin/look-after-it/privacy-audit"},"657":{"id":"/docs/admin/look-after-it/privacy-audit-0","page_id":"/docs/admin/look-after-it/privacy-audit","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/admin/look-after-it/privacy-audit","content":"Every outside address Home can contact, when, and what it sends."},"658":{"id":"/docs/admin/look-after-it/privacy-audit-1","page_id":"/docs/admin/look-after-it/privacy-audit","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/admin/look-after-it/privacy-audit#-what-can-leave-the-house","content":"🌍 What can leave the house"},"659":{"id":"/docs/admin/look-after-it/privacy-audit-2","page_id":"/docs/admin/look-after-it/privacy-audit","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/admin/look-after-it/privacy-audit#-what-stays-on-your-network","content":"🏠 What stays on your network"},"660":{"id":"/docs/admin/look-after-it/privacy-audit-3","page_id":"/docs/admin/look-after-it/privacy-audit","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/admin/look-after-it/privacy-audit#-how-to-check-it-yourself","content":"✅ How to check it yourself"},"661":{"id":"/docs/admin/look-after-it/privacy-audit-4","page_id":"/docs/admin/look-after-it/privacy-audit","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/admin/look-after-it/privacy-audit","content":"Home runs in your house. Nothing leaves unless a row on this page says so. Open it at **Settings**, **Home settings**, **Privacy**, **What connects to the internet**, or **Settings**, **Data and privacy** for your own view."},"662":{"id":"/docs/admin/look-after-it/privacy-audit-5","page_id":"/docs/admin/look-after-it/privacy-audit","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/admin/look-after-it/privacy-audit","content":"The page is built from the code and each package's declared sources, so it cannot drift from what Home does. A row shows only while that feature is in use."},"663":{"id":"/docs/admin/look-after-it/privacy-audit-6","page_id":"/docs/admin/look-after-it/privacy-audit","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/admin/look-after-it/privacy-audit#-what-can-leave-the-house","content":"| Row                                              | When                                                                                                                         | What goes          |\n| ------------------------------------------------ | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ------------------ |\n| Model downloads (wake word, face, speech, robot) | Once per model, the first time a feature needs it. For the wake word, that is the first time someone switches it on in chat. | A download request |","table":"table-0"},"664":{"id":"/docs/admin/look-after-it/privacy-audit-7","page_id":"/docs/admin/look-after-it/privacy-audit","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/admin/look-after-it/privacy-audit#-what-can-leave-the-house","content":"| Row                   | When               | What goes             |\n| --------------------- | ------------------ | --------------------- |\n| Update check (GitHub) | At most once a day | Your internet address |","table":"table-0"},"665":{"id":"/docs/admin/look-after-it/privacy-audit-8","page_id":"/docs/admin/look-after-it/privacy-audit","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/admin/look-after-it/privacy-audit#-what-can-leave-the-house","content":"| Row                          | When                                   | What goes                                             |\n| ---------------------------- | -------------------------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------- |\n| Blocked-site index and lists | Index about daily, lists about monthly | Your internet address. Shown only while a list is on. |","table":"table-0"},"666":{"id":"/docs/admin/look-after-it/privacy-audit-9","page_id":"/docs/admin/look-after-it/privacy-audit","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/admin/look-after-it/privacy-audit#-what-can-leave-the-house","content":"| Row            | When          | What goes                                                                                                 |\n| -------------- | ------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| Internet check | Once a minute | A DNS lookup of example.com and an empty connection to 1.1.1.1:443. Turn it off under **Internet check**. |","table":"table-0"},"667":{"id":"/docs/admin/look-after-it/privacy-audit-10","page_id":"/docs/admin/look-after-it/privacy-audit","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/admin/look-after-it/privacy-audit#-what-can-leave-the-house","content":"| Row        | When                                                  | What goes                         |\n| ---------- | ----------------------------------------------------- | --------------------------------- |\n| News feeds | About every 30 minutes at most, while the shelf is on | A plain request for the feed file |","table":"table-0"},"668":{"id":"/docs/admin/look-after-it/privacy-audit-11","page_id":"/docs/admin/look-after-it/privacy-audit","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/admin/look-after-it/privacy-audit#-what-can-leave-the-house","content":"| Row                     | When                                  | What goes          |\n| ----------------------- | ------------------------------------- | ------------------ |\n| Reference books (Kiwix) | When an adult installs or updates one | A download request |","table":"table-0"},"669":{"id":"/docs/admin/look-after-it/privacy-audit-12","page_id":"/docs/admi