 words and more room."],[884,"**Contributors only.** Architecture, how to build, and generated reference."],[12,"**Control a smart-home device**: type the Home Assistant domain, the service and the entity id."],[1035,"**Copy**: copies the reply."],[54,"**Daily help**: timer, reminders, lists, weather, currency, unit conversion, math, translation"],[694,"**Dismiss** asks you to confirm, then hides the item."],[110,"**Encyclopedia lookups** and **Web searches** (advanced) can each follow the household choice or override it. Children and teens keep their protections in every mode."],[594,"**Engines** says \"No Stack configured\" when no engine is set. Open **Where the engine runs**, pick one, and run **Check the connection**. The page for the Home computer is at Troubleshooting."],[588,"**Engines** shows **Engine health** and a **Check the connection** button."],[1298,"**Family**: one card for each person. Tap a card to open that person's profile, where memories live."],[210,"**For the technical dad.** How things work, how to set them up, how to look after and support them. No code internals; for those, see For developers."],[749,"**Go back** returns to the previous version after you confirm."],[1037,"**Helpful**: tells MaiPai the answer was good."],[57,"**Home control**: lights on and off, lock doors"],[375,"**Home** settings are set once for the household. **Person** settings belong to one person, and the guardian rules decide who may change them for a child or teen. Level is **basic**, **advanced** or **expert**; the app hides higher levels until asked. A blank \"What it does\" means the screen explains it in place. Settings marked \"Not active yet\" are saved but nothing reads them today. Robot and vision settings (keys starting `robot.`, `person.robot.`, `person.vision.` and `vision.`) are used by MaiPai Bot, not by Home itself."],[1295,"**Home**: counts for people, updates and repairs, and recent activity."],[169,"**Household settings** are writable only by an owner or admin."],[55,"**Info**: news, sports, web search, media lookup, almanac (date, time, moon, holidays, on this day)"],[1006,"**Instructions** shape the answers in that project."],[1020,"**Large**: bigger words and buttons, stronger contrast."],[653,"**Layers** says \"No traced turns yet\" until a turn has left a timing trace."],[56,"**Learning and play**: tutor, trivia, jokes, bedtime storybook, music"],[1297,"**Library**: the files you and the family have added."],[58,"**Memory**: remember and recall"],[1040,"**More**: more choices. Adults and teens can pick **Remember this** to keep a fact."],[590,"**Needs restart** or **Update available** on a row means exactly that."],[59,"**News feeds**: household feeds and kids' feeds"],[1038,"**Not helpful**: opens a short form."],[1036,"**Read aloud**: reads it to you."],[1039,"**Refresh**: asks for a new answer."],[11,"**Say something back**: type what MaiPai says, and optionally a spoken version."],[170,"**Session lock** (ask for the PIN again after idle time) is set by an owner or admin, from the people list in Settings, Users."],[1021,"**Simple**: bigger buttons, calm colors and helpers."],[1018,"**Standard**: MaiPai as it comes."],[34,"**Telegram me about new Repairs items**"],[36,"**Telegram me when a MaiPai Home update is available**"],[38,"**Telegram me when a model download fails**"],[37,"**Telegram me when a Stack engine reports an open warning or critical problem**"],[35,"**Telegram me when backups start failing**"],[1334,"**This computer.** Home starts the AI engine install right away. A progress bar at the bottom of the wizard shows each step: fetch, build and start, then the model downloads. You can keep answering questions while it works."],[726,"**Turn trace** shows only for owners and admins, and not in an Incognito chat. You can also open `/trace/` followed by a turn's id on your Home address."],[1225,"**Welcome. Pick a topic and follow the steps.**"],[865,"`areas` names code groups defined once at the top of the file, each a list of globs."],[868,"`baseline` is the commit the docs were last verified at, used until a `v*` tag exists."],[959,"`bun scripts/docsDrift.ts --check` runs the same completeness check by hand."],[866,"`covers` adds extra globs for one page (for example `docs/design/RULES.md`)."],[867,"`ignore` lists globs that never count as a change: tests, locales, docs."],[330,"`install.sh --stack-only` fetches, builds and starts the Stack, writes `engines.stack.url`, and records its progress in `data/stack-install.json` (state, stage, a plain problem). Home reads that file for the wizard bar. On macOS Home is a root daemon and runs the step itself. On Linux Home is an unprivileged user, so the installer adds a one-shot unit, `maipai-stack-install.service`, and a sudoers rule that allows exactly `systemctl start --no-block maipai-stack-install.service` for the Home user. The `scripts/` folder is root-owned so that user cannot change what the unit runs. The step is safe to run again."],[1189,"<Callout type=\"info\">Away from home, MaiPai only opens if an admin set up remote access.</Callout>"],[1306,"<Callout type=\"info\">Some settings show a lock. A lock means an admin controls that one.</Callout>"],[1398,"<Callout type=\"info\">Teens, children and guests may not need a PIN. Adults always do.</Callout>"],[1118,"<Callout type=\"info\">The microphone works only while the page is open and you have allowed it.</Callout>"],[147,"<Callout type=\"info\">The sidebar in some screenshots still says People. That page is now called Family.</Callout>"],[1026,"<Callout type=\"info\">These choices change comfort only. They never change what is safe or allowed.</Callout>"],[1450,"<Callout type=\"info\">These lists are for the household. They do not read any chat.</Callout>"],[883,"<Callout type=\"warn\" title=\"Table of contents draft\">Kept small on purpose. Written after the User and Admin guides are signed off.</Callout>"],[941,"<Callout type=\"warn\" title=\"Table