estore** banner appears. Restart Home."],[603,"A backup is one encrypted copy of Home's household database: people, memories, conversations and settings. Models, engines, the reference library and uploaded files are not in it. Those are downloaded or copied again after a restore."],[608,"A backup on the same disk as Home does not survive that disk failing. Copy the `backups` folder to another disk or computer regularly."],[1128,"A box called \"What Incognito does\" appears the first time. Tap **Got it**."],[960,"A change in meaning that touches no listed file (a new rule). Someone still has to say \"this affects the docs\"."],[171,"A child's **Sensitive subjects** levels are set only by an owner or admin. The child cannot change them."],[829,"A child's hard-moment notice to adults. See Add people."],[675,"A child's or teen's search words never go to DuckDuckGo or Brave."],[6,"A command fires only on the exact phrase. It never guesses."],[1358,"A daily job keeps each log file under about 20 MB. It keeps the last three older copies."],[1285,"A feature can send the small piece it needs, such as your search words or the place for a weather check. A web search sends the words you searched, never your name or address. A child's or teen's search never goes to DuckDuckGo or Brave, and it follows the household **Search sources** choice."],[202,"A folder that looks stray may be live household data. Open it first and check what it holds. Never delete `records` or `keys` without a backup and the backup key."],[1142,"A greyed-out or locked setting was set by an admin. You cannot change it. The row says who to ask."],[256,"A list of tested computers."],[848,"A lock means the setting belongs to the age group or the person. Ask the owner, or read the help text under the setting. A teen's own settings are not yours to change."],[1340,"A Mac that runs Home all day works best with a few settings changed. Setup shows them as a list. You can also run the tool yourself at the Mac. It changes nothing unless you add `--yes`."],[1322,"A Mac with Apple silicon or Intel, and an internet connection."],[958,"A new page or picture gets its entry in `docs-covers.json` in the same commit. A test fails if one is missing or points at nothing."],[1370,"A private AI helper that lives on a computer in your house."],[1221,"A red bar that says \"Listening for Hey Jarvis\" shows while it is on. Tap **Turn off wake word listening** to stop it."],[624,"A restore you have never tried is a guess. Once, on a spare computer, install Home, restore a backup with your saved key and sign in."],[1480,"A role is a label that sets what a person may do: **Owner**, **Admin**, **Adult**, **Teen**, **Child** or **Guest**. See What each role can do."],[976,"A search sends only your search words, with no name or address. The Privacy page explains it. See What stays in the house."],[60,"A shelf of apps on the Home screen is planned, not available yet."],[1453,"A short table of the six roles and what each one may do."],[66,"A signed catalog index check, so a tampered catalog is rejected."],[712,"A storage summary."],[1466,"A teen's chats and settings stay private from admins."],[1415,"A teen's profile, memories and settings are private. A parent gets no check-in view of a teen."],[725,"A trace holds names and timings only. It has no message text, no tool details and no names of people. A turn from a temporary or Incognito chat has no trace."],[754,"Add a person, pick a role, and set a child's time limits and storage."],[1043,"Add a short note if you like. It is optional."],[45,"Add and remove packages"],[220,"Add people and parental controls"],[753,"Add people and parental controls"],[285,"Add your family: Add people."],[203,"Admin guide 🛠️"],[943,"Admin guideFor the person who runs it. 18 pages."],[1176,"Admins also see **Error details** on a failed answer. Send those to whoever helps with the house."],[1199,"Admins can build a support report to share when asking for help. See Troubles