e hard rules, with links to the authority file."],[65,"The Home server already has the groundwork:"],[948,"The idea in one line"],[337,"The installer clears the quarantine flag on the install folder and checks the signature of Bun and the Stack binary. An unsigned binary gets an ad-hoc signature, which Apple silicon requires. If macOS still blocks one, choose Allow Anyway in System Settings, Privacy and Security."],[577,"The installer creates a `maipai-stack` service user, installs the Stack under `/opt/maipai-stack`, keeps its data in `/data/stack`, and enables SSH, asking first if `openssh-server` is missing. It then installs the `maipai-engine` tool."],[332,"The installer installs the **latest published release**, never the main branch. If no release exists it stops with \"could not find a published release ... there is nothing to install\". Run from source until one does. `--version v0.1.0` installs a named release. Choose a setup plan with `--plan recommended`, `--plan moderate` or `--plan minimal`; the wizard reads it later."],[316,"The installer runs Home in the background so it survives a reboot with nobody signed in. For the short, step by step version for the household, see the install, upgrade, uninstall and fix page."],[799,"The left column shows the global defaults. Tick or untick a box in the person's column."],[315,"The log is `data/local-app/app.log`."],[146,"The main menu has **Home**, **Chat**, **Family**, **Privacy** and **Settings**. Admin work lives under **Settings**, in the **Home settings** area. Backups, Updates, Repairs, Status, Storage and Engines are pages you reach from Settings."],[1294,"The main menu runs down the left side on a computer. On a phone it stays as the same thin column of icons. It always has the same items."],[614,"The new copy appears in the table with its date and size."],[1449,"The news shelf has its own card where you choose which news sources show up. It sits beside the blocked sites card."],[806,"The News shelf on Home is on by default. Pick which feed lists each age group sees:"],[652,"The numbers come from what Home already records. Nothing new is collected, and nothing leaves the house."],[1220,"The only wake word is \"Hey Jarvis\". Allow the microphone in your browser, and keep the MaiPai page open."],[280,"The owner can add everyone else, including admins. See People, roles and permissions."],[662,"The page is built from the code and each package's declared sources, so it cannot drift from what Home does. A row shows only while that feature is in use."],[127,"The parts of a MaiPai Home, what each one does, and where it runs."],[137,"The person types or speaks in the browser."],[768,"The person's age group follows the role. A child gets child controls, a teen gets teen controls. See People, roles and permissions."],[955,"The release step then updates only that list. Pictures from the docs run are retaken with `DOCS_SHOTS_ONLY`, so nothing else is regenerated."],[804,"The same pair exists for child, teen and adult."],[1300,"The search box at the top finds chats, people and pages."],[573,"The second computer runs Ubuntu Linux. Other systems are not supported for this."],[1117,"The setting belongs to this device, not to you. Listening is paused while a voice conversation is open and stops when you close the page."],[260,"The setup wizard screen by screen, and what is not built yet."],[149,"The six roles, what each can do, and what an admin can never see."],[296,"The Stack step"],[199,"The Storage page shows what each person uses and the caps."],[1254,"The things MaiPai keeps in your house, always."],[1333,"The wizard asks where the AI runs."],[284,"The wizard says how many things are left. They are in the setup checklist on the Home screen, such as adding family, enabling away access and saving the backup key. Come back to them at your own pace."],[977,"Their searches follow the house settings, and what MaiPai reads is checked first."],[283,"Then press **Open my Home**."],[14